// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  POST /schools/current/academic-years/{year}/classes/{id}/sections
// Needs X-School-Subdomain, a year, and a class id from Create Class.
//
//  sectionNo CAN NEVER BE CHANGED. There is no rename endpoint and there must
//  not be one: eight collections store it as a plain string, and a section is
//  EMBEDDED so it has no id for them to reference instead.
//
//  IT IS BOTH THE REFERENCE AND THE DISPLAY VALUE, which is why ClassSection
//  has no separate name field. Uniqueness folds case; storage does not.
//
//  THE DUPLICATE CHECK IS THE ONLY GUARD. Mongo cannot make an array's
//  contents unique, so there is no index to fall back on.
//
//  capacity IS A PLAN, NOT A LIMIT. Nothing enforces it. 0 is refused.
//
//  classTeacherDocsId IS CHECKED AGAINST THIS SCHOOL. Another school's real
//  staff id is a 404, not an accepted teacher.
// =========================================================================
//
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 01  ADD A SECTION                                      -> 201 Created
//     The body above.
//     OUT: the class's WHOLE section list, with sectionCount and activeCount.
//     A student can be placed in it as soon as the student module exists.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 02  JUST A NUMBER                                      -> 201 Created
//     capacity and classTeacherDocsId are both optional. A section with no
//     class teacher is a real state, not an incomplete one.
//
//     {
//       "sectionNo": "B"
//     }
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 03  A DUPLICATE                                        -> 409 Conflict
//     Send case 01 again.
//     OUT: { "code": "SECTION_ALREADY_EXISTS" }
//     Checked in the service — Mongo cannot make an array unique.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 04  THE SAME NUMBER IN LOWER CASE                      -> 409 Conflict
//     "a" is not a second section. Uniqueness folds case; storage does not.
//
//     {
//       "sectionNo": "a"
//     }
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 05  A SECTION NAMED BY COLOUR                          -> 201 Created
//     No shape is imposed. sectionNo is the display value as well as the
//     reference, so it is stored exactly as typed — trimmed, nothing else.
//
//     {
//       "sectionNo": "Blue",
//       "capacity": 35
//     }
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 06  A CAPACITY OF ZERO                                 -> 400 Bad Request
//     @Min(1). A section nobody can be placed in is not a section.
//     Absent is fine and means no plan was recorded.
//
//     {
//       "sectionNo": "Z",
//       "capacity": 0
//     }
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 07  A CLASS TEACHER                                    -> 201 Created
//     A real Staff.id belonging to THIS school. There is no API that creates
//     staff yet — the people module has none — so insert one directly to try it.
//
//     {
//       "sectionNo": "C",
//       "classTeacherDocsId": "67aa15d9dc3f7d0011111111"
//     }
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 08  ANOTHER SCHOOL'S TEACHER                           -> 404 Not Found
//     A REAL staff id belonging to a different school.
//     OUT: { "code": "STAFF_NOT_FOUND" }
//     The lookup is findByIdAndSchoolId — existing is not enough.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 09  NO SECTION NUMBER                                  -> 400 Bad Request
//     OUT: { "code": "VALIDATION_FAILED", fieldErrors: { sectionNo: ... } }
//
//     {
//       "capacity": 40
//     }
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 10  A REAL CLASS ID UNDER THE WRONG YEAR               -> 404 Not Found
//     Keep the class id, change the year to another this school has.
//     OUT: { "code": "CLASS_NOT_FOUND" } — the year scopes the lookup.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 11  A YEAR THAT HAS BEEN ENDED                         -> 409 Conflict
//     Run POST /academic-years/{name}/end first.
//     OUT: { "code": "ACADEMIC_YEAR_NOT_RUNNING" } — gate 4.
//     Then list the classes: a suspended or closed year still READS fine.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  REFUSALS
//     400 VALIDATION_FAILED                No sectionNo, a blank one, one over 20 characters, or a capacity below 1.
//     400 TENANT_NOT_RESOLVED              The X-School-Subdomain header is missing or blank.
//     404 SCHOOL_NOT_FOUND                 No school has that subdomain.
//     404 ACADEMIC_YEAR_NOT_FOUND          The {year} in the path is not a year of this school.
//     404 CLASS_NOT_FOUND                  No class with that id in that year — including a real id under the wrong year, or another school's.
//     404 STAFF_NOT_FOUND                  No such staff in this school, including another school's real id.
//     409 SECTION_ALREADY_EXISTS           That class already has a section with that number, case folded. A retired one counts.
//     409 SCHOOL_NOT_ACTIVE                Gate 1 — the school is suspended, closed or deleted.
//     409 SUBSCRIPTION_NOT_USABLE          Gate 2 — expired, suspended, or the period has ended.
//     409 ACADEMIC_YEAR_NOT_RUNNING        Gate 4 — the year was ended by POST .../end.

