//  THE FOUR FILTERS A PICKER ACTUALLY WANTS ARE NOT HERE: ?employed=,
//  ?departmentDocsId=, ?positionDocsId=, ?employmentType= all live on
//  EmploymentRecord, which #16 writes and which does not exist. IGNORED, not
//  refused — accepting them would be a filter that silently matches nothing.
//
//  SORTED BY fullName, TIEBROKEN BY employeeNo — two people share a name.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  EVERYBODY                        -> 200 OK   no parameters
// 02  ?search=anita                    -> 200 OK   name, case-insensitive
// 03  ?search=000001                   -> 200 OK   the employee number too
// 04  ?search=Sharma(                  -> 200 OK   empty page, NOT a 500
// 05  ?hasEmail=false                  -> 200 OK   who is missing contact details
// 06  ?gender=MALE / ?gender=ROBOT     -> 200 / 400
// 07  ?nationalityCode=in              -> 200 OK   matches IN
// 08  ?hasEmail=true&hasPhone=true     -> 200 OK   AND-ed
// 09  ?employed=true                   -> 200 OK   IGNORED, narrows nothing
// 10  ?page=0&size=2, then page 1      -> 200 OK   totalElements counts all
// 11  ?page=-1 / ?size=0 / ?size=101   -> 400      refused, never clamped
// 12  ?size=1 walked to the end        -> 200 OK   everybody exactly once
// 13  ?sort=dateOfBirth                -> 400      a hidden field is not sortable
// 14  a suspended school               -> 200 OK   no gate runs on a read
//
//  EVERY REFUSAL
//     400 INVALID_PAGE / INVALID_PAGE_SIZE / INVALID_SORT_FIELD
//     400 TENANT_NOT_RESOLVED              Header missing or blank.
//     404 SCHOOL_NOT_FOUND                 No school has that subdomain.

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  PATCH /schools/current/staff/{id}
// Every field optional. Needs X-School-Subdomain and a staff id.
//
//  IT EDITS THE WHOLE PROFILE. The plan split this across four endpoints —
//  this one plus PUT /addresses (#3), /emergency-contact (#4) and /photo
//  (#5). Folded into one on 2026-09-15.
//
//  AN ADDRESS AND THE EMERGENCY CONTACT ARE REPLACED WHOLE, NEVER MERGED.
//  Send the object and it BECOMES the object; anything you leave out is gone.
//  That is the reasoning #3 and #4 existed for, kept: half a changed address
//  is a delivery to the wrong place, and a contact with a new name beside an
//  old number is worse than no contact.
//
//  {} CLEARS an address or the contact. "" clears the photo. "" on the name,
//  phone or email is REFUSED — all three are required.
//
//  nationalityCode and preferredLanguage are CORRECTABLE BUT NOT CLEARABLE:
//  they are enums, "" is not one of their values, and null already means
//  "leave it alone". JsonNullable would fix it; we do not depend on it.
//
//  NEVER employeeNo — generated and printed on things. Nothing about the job
//  either; that is EmploymentRecord and #16.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  A RENAME                         -> 200  the whole person, in #8's shape
// 02  {}                               -> 400  NOTHING_TO_UPDATE
// 03  { "fullName": "   " }            -> 400  STAFF_NAME_REQUIRED
// 04  AN ADDRESS REPLACES WHOLE        -> 200  send only a city after a full
//                                             address: the rest is GONE
// 05  { "currentAddress": {} }         -> 200  clears it
// 06  THE EMERGENCY CONTACT, WHOLE     -> 200  same rule
// 07  { "profileImageDocsId": "" }     -> 200  clears the photo
// 08  THEIR OWN NUMBER                 -> 200  not a duplicate
// 09  SOMEBODY ELSE'S NUMBER           -> 409  STAFF_PHONE_TAKEN, and a good
//                                             name sent with it does NOT land
// 10  { "nationalityCode": "12" }      -> 400  INVALID_VALUE
// 11  { "employeeNo": "..." }          -> 200  IGNORED, the number stays
// 12  ANOTHER SCHOOL'S PERSON          -> 404  STAFF_NOT_FOUND
//
//  EVERY REFUSAL
//     400 NOTHING_TO_UPDATE / STAFF_NAME_REQUIRED
//     400 STAFF_PHONE_REQUIRED / STAFF_EMAIL_REQUIRED   Neither can be cleared.
//     400 INVALID_VALUE                Not a country, or not a supported locale.
//     400 TENANT_NOT_RESOLVED          Header missing or blank.
//     403 SCHOOL_NOT_ACTIVE            Gate 1. Reads still work.
//     404 STAFF_NOT_FOUND              Not a staff member of this school.
//     409 STAFF_PHONE_TAKEN / STAFF_EMAIL_TAKEN         Somebody ELSE holds it.

{
    "fullName": "Anita Verma"
}

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  GET /schools/current/staff/{id}
// A GET — no body. Needs X-School-Subdomain and a staff id.
//
//  THE FULLEST THING THIS PRODUCT RETURNS ABOUT A HUMAN BEING. A date of
//  birth, two addresses, an emergency contact. #7's row carries none of it
//  precisely so this one can: a list is read by every dropdown, this by one
//  page.
//
//  AND NOTHING CHECKS WHO IS ASKING. The module plan calls authorization its
//  open item that matters most, and this is the endpoint it means. The
//  response repeats it in `note` on every read.
//
//  THE EMPLOYMENT BLOCK IS ABSENT — not null, not {}. #16 writes the record
//  and is not built; there is no employment_records collection at all.
//  employmentNote says so, because an absence like that otherwise reads as a
//  bug in the caller's own code.
//
//  AND THAT IS NOT SCAFFOLDING. A person with no employment record stays a
//  real state once #16 exists — entered but not yet hired, which is what #1
//  leaves them in.
//
//  SCOPED BY schoolId, never by id alone. An unscoped lookup here does not
//  leak a name, it leaks a home address.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  ONE PERSON IN FULL               -> 200 OK   everything #1 stored
// 02  WHAT #7 HIDES AND #8 SHOWS       -> 200 OK   compare against the list row
// 03  ONLY THE REQUIRED FIELDS         -> 200 OK   absent keys, never null
// 04  THE EMPLOYMENT BLOCK             -> 200 OK   no key at all; note says why
// 05  ANOTHER SCHOOL'S PERSON          -> 404      says NOTHING about them
// 06  A PADDED ID                      -> 200 OK   trimmed before the lookup
// 07  A SUSPENDED SCHOOL               -> 200 OK   no gate runs on a read
//
//  EVERY REFUSAL
//     400 TENANT_NOT_RESOLVED              The X-School-Subdomain header is missing or blank.
//     404 SCHOOL_NOT_FOUND                 No school has that subdomain.
//     404 STAFF_NOT_FOUND                  Not a staff member of this school.

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  PATCH /schools/current/employment/{id}
// Every field optional. Needs X-School-Subdomain and an EMPLOYMENT record id
// — NOT a staff id. Somebody has several records; the URL says which.
//
//  A CORRECTION, NOT AN EVENT. A promotion or transfer is #16, a resignation
//  is #17; both move two things at once. This fixes what was TYPED WRONG on a
//  record that already describes the right thing.
//
//  NEVER current. A PATCH that could set it is exactly how two records end up
//  current — or NONE do, which is worse, because the person then reads as
//  unemployed. The partial index catches the first; nothing catches the second.
//
//  NEVER positionDocsId. Moving somebody to another position is a TRANSFER,
//  which is a new record, which is #16. Editing it in place would rewrite
//  where they worked last year.
//
//  A CURRENT RECORD CANNOT BE ENDED OR TERMINATED HERE — both are #17, which
//  sets current and a terminal status TOGETHER. A CLOSED record may have both
//  corrected, which is what this endpoint is for.
//
//  MOVING A DATE IS CHECKED AGAINST THE NEIGHBOURS, and no index does that:
//  school_staff_employment_start_uniq forbids two records STARTING on one day,
//  and nothing compares a start to the previous record's END. A gap is
//  allowed; an overlap is not.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  { "managerDocsId": "..." }        -> 200  "" clears it
// 02  status + employmentType           -> 200  employmentType is NOT in the
//                                              plan's list; added because a
//                                              typo there has no other fix
// 03  {}                                -> 400  NOTHING_TO_UPDATE
// 04  { "current": false, ... }         -> 200  IGNORED; still current
// 05  { "positionDocsId": "...", ... }  -> 200  IGNORED; does not move
// 06  { "status": "TERMINATED" }        -> 400  on a CURRENT record
// 07  { "effectiveUntil": "..." }       -> 400  on a CURRENT record
// 08  an end before its own start       -> 400  EMPLOYMENT_ENDS_BEFORE_IT_STARTS
// 09  the same start as another record  -> 409  EMPLOYMENT_ALREADY_STARTS_THEN
// 10  moved back onto the previous one  -> 409  EMPLOYMENT_OVERLAPS_PREVIOUS
// 11  a start well after the previous   -> 200  a GAP is allowed
// 12  another school's record           -> 404  EMPLOYMENT_NOT_FOUND
//
//  EVERY REFUSAL
//     400 NOTHING_TO_UPDATE                 Nothing editable was sent.
//     400 EMPLOYMENT_STATUS_TERMINAL        TERMINATED on a current record.
//     400 EMPLOYMENT_CURRENT_CANNOT_END     An end date on a current record.
//     400 EMPLOYMENT_ENDS_BEFORE_IT_STARTS  The dates would run backwards.
//     400 PROBATION_BEFORE_START            Probation before the start.
//     400 MANAGER_IS_SELF                   Nobody manages themselves.
//     400 TENANT_NOT_RESOLVED               Header missing or blank.
//     403 SCHOOL_NOT_ACTIVE                 Gate 1.
//     404 EMPLOYMENT_NOT_FOUND / MANAGER_NOT_FOUND
//     409 EMPLOYMENT_ALREADY_STARTS_THEN    Another record begins that day.
//     409 EMPLOYMENT_OVERLAPS_PREVIOUS      It would land on an earlier record.

{
    "managerDocsId": "{{staffDocsId}}"
}

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  POST /schools/current/employment/{id}/status
// Needs X-School-Subdomain and an EMPLOYMENT record id. status is required.
//
//  A STATUS CHANGE IS AN EVENT, NOT A CORRECTION. #18 fixes what was typed
//  wrong; this records something that HAPPENED to somebody. What a school
//  needs six months later is the REASON, not the new value — and a field on
//  a general PATCH cannot demand one. That is why status left #18 on
//  2026-09-16.
//
//  FIVE OF THE SEVEN REQUIRE A REASON, and the ENUM decides rather than a
//  list in the service, so a status added later brings its own answer:
//
//     PROBATION      no reason needed   a normal start
//     ACTIVE         no reason needed   the ordinary state
//     ON_LEAVE       REQUIRED           how long, backfill, paid?
//     SUSPENDED      REQUIRED
//     NOTICE_PERIOD  REQUIRED           whose decision was it
//     TERMINATED     REQUIRED           and ends the employment
//     RETIRED        REQUIRED           and ends the employment
//
//  A REASON IS KEPT where it is not required too — "Passed probation" beside
//  ACTIVE is worth having.
//
//  OFFERED WAS REMOVED from the enum on 2026-09-16; "accepted an offer, has
//  not started" is now a record with a FUTURE effectiveFrom. RETIRED was
//  added, kept apart from TERMINATED because a school reads them differently.
//
//  A TERMINAL STATUS ENDS THE EMPLOYMENT in the same write — current:false
//  plus effectiveUntil, defaulting to today. It HAS to: terminal and current
//  at once is a contradiction nothing in the model prevents. This absorbed
//  #17 POST /staff/{id}/separate.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  ON_LEAVE + reason                 -> 200  still current
// 02  ON_LEAVE, no reason               -> 400  EMPLOYMENT_STATUS_REASON_REQUIRED
//                                              (a BLANK reason counts as none)
// 03  ACTIVE, no reason                 -> 200  neither of the two needs one
// 04  ACTIVE + reason                   -> 200  KEPT, not discarded
// 05  RETIRED + reason + effectiveUntil -> 200  current:false, separationReason set
// 06  TERMINATED + reason, no date      -> 200  effectiveUntil defaults to TODAY
// 07  terminal + a date before the start-> 400  EMPLOYMENT_ENDS_BEFORE_IT_STARTS
// 08  the status it already has         -> 409  EMPLOYMENT_STATUS_UNCHANGED
// 09  a record already closed           -> 409  EMPLOYMENT_NOT_CURRENT
// 10  OFFERED                           -> 400  removed from the enum
// 11  another school's record           -> 404  EMPLOYMENT_NOT_FOUND
//
//  EVERY REFUSAL
//     400 EMPLOYMENT_STATUS_REASON_REQUIRED   The status needs one.
//     400 EMPLOYMENT_ENDS_BEFORE_IT_STARTS    A terminal date before the start.
//     400 VALIDATION_FAILED                   status absent or not one of the seven.
//     400 TENANT_NOT_RESOLVED                 Header missing or blank.
//     403 SCHOOL_NOT_ACTIVE                   Gate 1.
//     404 EMPLOYMENT_NOT_FOUND                Not this school's record.
//     409 EMPLOYMENT_STATUS_UNCHANGED         Already at that status.
//     409 EMPLOYMENT_NOT_CURRENT              The record has closed; next is #16.

{
    "status": "ON_LEAVE",
    "reason": "Maternity leave until March"
}

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  GET /schools/current/staff/{id}/employment
// A GET — no body. Needs X-School-Subdomain and a STAFF id (not a record id).
//
//  AN UNKNOWN PERSON IS A 404, NOT AN EMPTY LIST. That is what this endpoint
//  is built on. Without reading the staff record first, an id belonging to
//  nobody would answer with [] — and "never employed" and "no such person"
//  would be indistinguishable. One is a normal state; the other is a bug in
//  whatever built the URL.
//
//  NEWEST FIRST. "What do they do now" is the common question and "what did
//  they do in 2019" is the rare one. The current record is MARKED on the row
//  as well, so nothing is inferred from position.
//
//  AN ENVELOPE, NOT A BARE ARRAY. currentlyEmployed and totalRecords are
//  questions a caller would otherwise answer by scanning the list, and an
//  array cannot grow a field without breaking every caller.
//
//  NOT PAGED. Nobody has a hundred employment records.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  A WHOLE CAREER                    -> 200  employ, then promote twice.
//                                              Three records newest first,
//                                              exactly one current, each
//                                              closed one ending the day
//                                              before the next began.
// 02  SOMEBODY NEVER EMPLOYED           -> 200  records [], totalRecords 0,
//                                              currentlyEmployed false, and a
//                                              note saying it is a REAL state.
// 03  AN UNKNOWN PERSON                 -> 404  STAFF_NOT_FOUND, NOT [].
//                                              Compare against 02 — those two
//                                              answers must differ.
// 04  AFTER A RETIREMENT                -> 200  the record stays, marked
//                                              current:false with its
//                                              separationReason;
//                                              currentlyEmployed false.
// 05  ANOTHER SCHOOL'S PERSON           -> 404  and ours read from their
//                                              subdomain is a 404 too.
// 06  A SUSPENDED SCHOOL                -> 200  no gate runs on a read.
//
//  EVERY REFUSAL
//     400 TENANT_NOT_RESOLVED              The X-School-Subdomain header is missing or blank.
//     404 SCHOOL_NOT_FOUND                 No school has that subdomain.
//     404 STAFF_NOT_FOUND                  Not a staff member of this school.

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  POST /schools/current/staff/{id}/employment
// Needs X-School-Subdomain and a staff id. positionDocsId, status,
// employmentType and effectiveFrom are required.
//
//  THE WRITE THE WHOLE PRODUCT WAS WAITING ON. #9 and #13 built the seat, #1
//  built the person, and nothing joined them — so nobody was employed
//  anywhere, #7 had no employment filters and #8 returned no employment.
//
//  ONE ENDPOINT BECAUSE IT IS ONE EVENT. Hire, promote and transfer all close
//  the record that was current and open a new one. Three endpoints doing that
//  would be three chances to leave TWO current — or NONE, which is worse,
//  because the person then reads as unemployed. Both halves come back.
//
//  @Transactional, AND THE MANAGER IS REGISTERED. The plan says this project
//  has none — out of date. Close then insert, in one transaction; the unique
//  partial index on current:true is what forces that order.
//
//  THE END DATE IS COMPUTED, NEVER SENT — the day before the new one starts.
//  There is no effectiveUntil on this request at all.
//
//  POSITION_FULL IS A WARNING ON A 201, never a refusal: a twelfth teacher in
//  eleven seats has already happened. TERMINATED is REFUSED — current and
//  finished at once is a contradiction nothing downstream can read.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  THE HIRE                         -> 201  no "closed" key at all
// 02  THE PROMOTION                    -> 201  both halves; old one ends the
//                                             DAY BEFORE the new one starts
// 03  EXACTLY ONE IS EVER CURRENT      -> check employment_records in Mongo
// 04  status TERMINATED                -> 400  EMPLOYMENT_STATUS_TERMINAL
// 05  a retired seat                   -> 409  POSITION_NOT_ACTIVE
// 06  managerDocsId = the person       -> 400  MANAGER_IS_SELF
// 07  two records starting one day     -> 409  EMPLOYMENT_ALREADY_STARTS_THEN
// 08  starting before the current one  -> 409  EMPLOYMENT_STARTS_BEFORE_CURRENT
// 09  probationUntil before the start  -> 400  PROBATION_BEFORE_START
// 10  a third into a two-seat post     -> 201 WITH a warning
// 11  current / effectiveUntil sent    -> 201  IGNORED, not refused
// 12  a suspended school               -> 403  SCHOOL_NOT_ACTIVE
//
//  EVERY REFUSAL
//     400 EMPLOYMENT_STATUS_TERMINAL       Current and finished at once. Leaving is #17.
//     400 MANAGER_IS_SELF                  Nobody manages themselves.
//     400 PROBATION_BEFORE_START           Probation ends before the job starts.
//     400 TENANT_NOT_RESOLVED              Header missing or blank.
//     403 SCHOOL_NOT_ACTIVE                Gate 1.
//     404 STAFF_NOT_FOUND / POSITION_NOT_FOUND / MANAGER_NOT_FOUND
//     409 POSITION_NOT_ACTIVE              A retired seat.
//     409 EMPLOYMENT_ALREADY_STARTS_THEN   Closed records count too.
//     409 EMPLOYMENT_STARTS_BEFORE_CURRENT The close would end it before it began.

{
    "positionDocsId": "{{positionDocsId}}",
    "status": "ACTIVE",
    "employmentType": "FULL_TIME",
    "effectiveFrom": "2026-04-01"
}

{
  "departmentCode": "ACADEMICS",
  "name": "Academic Department",
  "description": "Curriculum and teaching operations."
}

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  POST /schools/current/departments
// Needs X-School-Subdomain. No year anywhere — an org chart outlives them.
//
//  THIS IS THE FIRST CALL of the people module. A position needs a
//  department; the write that employs somebody needs a position.
//
//  departmentCode IS GIVEN, NEVER DERIVED — the termCode rule. Stored
//  trimmed and UPPER-CASED, so "admin" and "ADMIN" are one code.
//
//  TWO UNITS MAY SHARE A NAME. Only the code is unique.
//
//  THE HEAD IS VALIDATED TO EXIST, NOT TO BE EMPLOYED. A school enters its
//  org chart before its employment records.
//
//  active IS NOT ACCEPTED. It starts true; retiring is #11. Sending it is
//  ignored, not refused.
//
//  NO GATE 4. There is no year in this path to ask it about.
// =========================================================================
//
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 01  A TOP-LEVEL UNIT                                    -> 201 Created
//     The body above.
//     OUT: departmentDocsId, active true, and NO parentDepartmentDocsId
//     field at all — absent, not null.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 02  THE CODE IS NORMALISED                              -> 201 Created
//     OUT: departmentCode is ADMIN — trimmed and upper-cased. The NAME does
//     not decide the code; they move independently.
//
//     { "departmentCode": "  admin  ", "name": "Administration" }
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 03  THE SAME CODE AGAIN                                 -> 409 Conflict
//     OUT: { "code": "DEPARTMENT_CODE_TAKEN" }
//     Case-folded, so sending "admin" after "ADMIN" is the same refusal.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 04  TWO UNITS SHARING A NAME                            -> 201 Created
//     Allowed — only the code is unique.
//
//     { "departmentCode": "ACADEMICS_2", "name": "Academic Department" }
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 05  NESTED UNDER ANOTHER                                -> 201 Created
//     { "departmentCode": "SCIENCE", "name": "Science",
//       "parentDepartmentDocsId": "{{departmentDocsId}}" }
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 06  AN UNKNOWN PARENT                                   -> 404 Not Found
//     OUT: { "code": "DEPARTMENT_NOT_FOUND" }
//     Another school's REAL department id is the same 404.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 07  A BLANK PARENT                                      -> 201 Created
//     "   " is treated as none, not as a lookup that fails.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 08  A HEAD WITH NO EMPLOYMENT RECORD                    -> 201 Created
//     A real Staff.id of this school. ACCEPTED ON PURPOSE.
//
//     { "departmentCode": "HEADED", "name": "Headed unit",
//       "headStaffDocsId": "67aa15d9dc3f7d0011111111" }
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 09  AN UNKNOWN HEAD                                     -> 404 Not Found
//     OUT: { "code": "STAFF_NOT_FOUND" }
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 10  THE FIELDS THIS ENDPOINT WILL NOT TAKE              -> 201 Created
//     active and schoolId are IGNORED, not refused.
//
//     { "departmentCode": "IGNORED", "name": "Ignored flags",
//       "active": false, "schoolId": "67aa15d9dc3f7d0099999999" }
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 11  A SUSPENDED SCHOOL                                  -> 409 Conflict
//     OUT: { "code": "SCHOOL_NOT_ACTIVE" } — gate 1.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 12  AFTER EVERY YEAR HAS ENDED                          -> 201 Created
//     STILL WORKS: gate 4 does not run here.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
//  EVERY REFUSAL
//     400 VALIDATION_FAILED                No departmentCode or name, either blank, a code over 40, or a name over 120.
//     400 TENANT_NOT_RESOLVED              The X-School-Subdomain header is missing or blank.
//     404 SCHOOL_NOT_FOUND                 No school has that subdomain.
//     404 DEPARTMENT_NOT_FOUND             The parent is not a department of this school.
//     404 STAFF_NOT_FOUND                  The head is not a staff member of this school.
//     409 DEPARTMENT_CODE_TAKEN            This school already uses that code, case-folded.
//     409 SCHOOL_NOT_ACTIVE                Gate 1 — the school is suspended, closed or deleted.
//     409 SUBSCRIPTION_NOT_USABLE          Gate 2 — expired, suspended, or the period has ended.

{
  "title": "Mathematics Teacher",
  "departmentDocsId": "{{departmentDocsId}}",
  "approvedHeadcount": 4,
  "teachingPosition": true
}

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  POST /schools/current/positions
// Needs X-School-Subdomain and an ACTIVE department id from Create Department.
//
//  A POSITION HAS NO CODE. positionCode was removed 2026-09-15; a seat is
//  addressed by its document id, which EmploymentRecord already stored. Its
//  unique index went with it — an index naming a field the model no longer
//  declares lets through exactly ONE row per school.
//
//  title IS UNIQUE WITHIN ITS DEPARTMENT — the job the code used to do. The
//  service folds case, the index does not, so the service is the stricter of
//  the two. A RETIRED SEAT KEEPS ITS TITLE.
//
//  THE DEPARTMENT MUST BE ACTIVE, not merely present.
//
//  THE REPORTING LINE MAY CROSS DEPARTMENTS, on purpose — the org tree and
//  the reporting line answer different questions.
//
//  approvedHeadcount FOLLOWS THE MODEL: absent or null becomes 1, and
//  "uncapped" is not storable because Position declares it @NotNull.
//
//  teachingPosition DEFAULTS FALSE. A department with no teaching seat gets
//  a WARNING, not a refusal.
// =========================================================================
//
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 01  A TEACHING SEAT                                     -> 201 Created
//     The body above. OUT: positionDocsId, active true, and NO positionCode
//     field — there is no such field any more.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 02  THE DEFAULTS                                        -> 201 Created
//     Only title and departmentDocsId.
//     OUT: approvedHeadcount 1, teachingPosition false.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 03  AN EXPLICIT NULL HEADCOUNT                          -> 201 Created
//     OUT: approvedHeadcount is 1, NOT uncapped.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 04  A HEADCOUNT OF ZERO                                 -> 400 Bad Request
//     @Min(1). A seat nobody may be hired into is not a seat.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 05  THE SAME TITLE AGAIN                                -> 409 Conflict
//     OUT: { "code": "POSITION_TITLE_TAKEN" }, naming the department.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 06  THE SAME TITLE IN ANOTHER CASE                      -> 409 Conflict
//     "mathematics teacher" after "Mathematics Teacher".
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 07  THE SAME TITLE IN ANOTHER DEPARTMENT                -> 201 Created
//     Uniqueness is scoped to the department, not the school.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 08  A RETIRED SEAT KEEPS ITS TITLE                      -> 409 Conflict
//     Set active:false on a seat in Mongo (#14 is not built), then send its
//     title again. The index does not filter on active, so neither does the
//     check.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 09  A RETIRED DEPARTMENT                                -> 409 Conflict
//     OUT: { "code": "DEPARTMENT_NOT_ACTIVE" } — not NOT_FOUND.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 10  AN UNKNOWN DEPARTMENT                               -> 404 Not Found
//     Another school's REAL department id is the same 404.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 11  A REPORTING LINE                                    -> 201 Created
//     { "title": "Junior Maths Teacher",
//       "departmentDocsId": "{{departmentDocsId}}",
//       "reportsToPositionDocsId": "{{positionDocsId}}" }
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 12  REPORTING ACROSS DEPARTMENTS                        -> 201 Created
//     ACCEPTED ON PURPOSE.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 13  AN UNKNOWN REPORTING LINE                           -> 404 Not Found
//     OUT: { "code": "POSITION_NOT_FOUND" }
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 14  A DEPARTMENT WITH NO TEACHING SEAT                  -> 201 Created
//     OUT: 201 WITH A WARNING. Add one teaching seat and later non-teaching
//     seats stop warning.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 15  AFTER EVERY YEAR HAS ENDED                          -> 201 Created
//     STILL WORKS: gate 4 does not run here.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
//  EVERY REFUSAL
//     400 VALIDATION_FAILED                No title or departmentDocsId, either blank, a title over 120, or approvedHeadcount below 1.
//     400 TENANT_NOT_RESOLVED              The X-School-Subdomain header is missing or blank.
//     404 SCHOOL_NOT_FOUND                 No school has that subdomain.
//     404 DEPARTMENT_NOT_FOUND             Not a department of this school.
//     404 POSITION_NOT_FOUND               The reporting line is not a position of this school.
//     409 DEPARTMENT_NOT_ACTIVE            The department exists but is retired.
//     409 POSITION_TITLE_TAKEN             That department already has that title, case-folded. Retired seats count.
//     409 SCHOOL_NOT_ACTIVE                Gate 1 — the school is suspended, closed or deleted.
//     409 SUBSCRIPTION_NOT_USABLE          Gate 2 — expired, suspended, or the period has ended.

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  PATCH /schools/current/positions/{id}
// Every field optional. Needs X-School-Subdomain and a position id.
//
//  ABSENT MEANS LEAVE IT ALONE, and an empty body is 400 NOTHING_TO_UPDATE.
//
//  NEVER departmentDocsId — A SEAT CANNOT MOVE DEPARTMENT. Editing it would
//  rewrite where every past holder worked, and every employment record under
//  the seat would silently change department too. A seat elsewhere is a NEW
//  seat. It is also what keeps school_department_title_uniq meaningful.
//
//  THIS IS THE ENDPOINT THAT CAN WRITE A REPORTING CYCLE, so this is where
//  the walk is — 409 POSITION_CYCLE. #13 needs none: a brand-new seat has
//  nothing reporting to it. The walk carries a visited set, so a cycle
//  ALREADY in the collection stops it rather than hanging the request.
//
//  THE TITLE CARRIES THE UNIQUENESS positionCode USED TO, scoped to the
//  department, RETIRED SEATS INCLUDED. Its own title in another case is a
//  correction, not a collision.
//
//  TURNING teachingPosition OFF is the interesting direction: it is how a
//  unit that had one teaching seat stops having any. Same warning #13 gives,
//  on the way out. A warning rides on a 200 — the seat is saved.
//
//  TWO CHECKS THE PLAN SPECIFIES AND THIS DOES NOT IMPLEMENT:
//  HEADCOUNT_BELOW_FILLED and 409 POSITION_STILL_FILLED. Neither can fire
//  yet — nothing writes an employment record, so the filled count could only
//  ever be zero. Both are owed the moment #16 lands.
// =========================================================================
//
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 01  A RETITLE                                           -> 200 OK
//     { "title": "Senior Mathematics Teacher" }
//     OUT: the new title, the department untouched.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 02  NOTHING AT ALL                                      -> 400 Bad Request
//     {}   OUT: { "code": "NOTHING_TO_UPDATE" }
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 03  ONLY THE DEPARTMENT                                 -> 400 Bad Request
//     { "departmentDocsId": "..." }
//     The same 400 — it is not on the request record, so the request is
//     empty. IGNORED on the way in, never refused. The seat does NOT move.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 04  THE TITLE CANNOT BE REMOVED                         -> 400 Bad Request
//     { "title": "   " }  OUT: { "code": "POSITION_TITLE_REQUIRED" }
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 05  A TITLE ANOTHER SEAT HOLDS                          -> 409 Conflict
//     Two seats in one unit; rename one to the other's title.
//     OUT: { "code": "POSITION_TITLE_TAKEN" } — and it FOLDS CASE, so
//     "academics ADMINISTRATOR" collides too.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 06  ITS OWN TITLE IN ANOTHER CASE                       -> 200 OK
//     { "title": "mathematics teacher" } on the seat already called
//     "Mathematics Teacher". Same seat, so a correction not a collision.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 07  A RETIRED SEAT STILL HOLDS ITS TITLE                -> 409 Conflict
//     Retire a seat in Mongo, then rename another to its title.
//     school_department_title_uniq does not filter on active, so a check
//     that skipped retired rows would accept a write the index refuses.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 08  CLEARING THE REPORTING LINE                         -> 200 OK
//     { "reportsToPositionDocsId": "" }
//     OUT: no reportsToPositionDocsId key — the seat reports to nobody.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 09  A SUPERVISOR IN ANOTHER DEPARTMENT                  -> 200 OK
//     Allowed deliberately. One Head of Safeguarding every unit reports to
//     is a real structure — the org tree and the reporting line answer
//     different questions.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 10  REPORTING TO ITSELF                                 -> 409 Conflict
//     OUT: { "code": "POSITION_CYCLE" } — the one-step case of the walk.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 11  A LOOP UP THE CHAIN                                 -> 409 Conflict
//     C reports to B reports to A. Make A report to C.
//     OUT: 409 POSITION_CYCLE — the walk goes up the WHOLE chain. Skipping
//     a level UPWARDS is fine and is not a cycle.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 12  THE HEADCOUNT                                       -> 200 OK / 400
//     8 raises it; 1 lowers it and nothing refuses that. 0 and -3 are a 400:
//     the model is @NotNull defaulting to 1, so null is NOT "uncapped".
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 13  TURNING OFF THE LAST TEACHING SEAT                  -> 200 OK
//     { "teachingPosition": false } on a unit's only teaching seat.
//     OUT: 200 WITH a warning. A warning is not a refusal — it is saved.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 14  RETIRING                                            -> 200 OK
//     { "active": false } — OUT: a nextStep saying it keeps its title,
//     because records made against it still name it. true restores.
//     Editing a RETIRED seat still works, as does one in a retired unit.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 15  ANOTHER SCHOOL'S SEAT                               -> 404 Not Found
//     A REAL position id belonging to a different school — as the seat
//     itself AND as the supervisor named. 404 POSITION_NOT_FOUND both ways.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
//  EVERY REFUSAL
//     400 NOTHING_TO_UPDATE                No editable field was sent.
//     400 POSITION_TITLE_REQUIRED          title sent blank.
//     400 TENANT_NOT_RESOLVED              The X-School-Subdomain header is missing or blank.
//     403 SCHOOL_NOT_ACTIVE                Gate 1 — suspended or closed. Reads still work.
//     404 SCHOOL_NOT_FOUND                 No school has that subdomain.
//     404 POSITION_NOT_FOUND               The seat, or the supervisor named, is not this school's.
//     409 POSITION_TITLE_TAKEN             Another seat in the unit holds it, retired included.
//     409 POSITION_CYCLE                   The proposed supervisor reports to this seat.

{
    "title": "Senior Mathematics Teacher"
}

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  GET /schools/current/departments?tree=&active=&search=&…
// A GET — no body. Needs X-School-Subdomain.
//
//  TWO SHAPES. ?tree=true gives nested roots; anything else gives a page
//  envelope. The caller picks, so it always knows which it is reading.
//
//  THE TREE CANNOT BE PAGED — 400 TREE_CANNOT_BE_PAGED, not a silently
//  dropped parameter. A page boundary cuts children off their parents, so
//  page 2 is not part of a chart — it is a broken one that looks like one.
//
//  THE ORPHAN CASE IS THE INTERESTING ONE. ?tree=true&active=true drops a
//  retired parent; its ACTIVE children are lifted to the top and marked
//  liftedToTop rather than vanishing with it.
//
//  FIVE FILTERS, ALL AND-ed: active, search (name OR code),
//  parentDepartmentDocsId, headStaffDocsId, topLevelOnly.
//
//  SORTED BY name, TIEBROKEN BY departmentCode — two units may share a name,
//  so name alone would put one row on two pages and another on none.
// =========================================================================
//
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 01  EVERY DEPARTMENT, FLAT                              -> 200 OK
//     No parameters. OUT: a page envelope, ordered by name then code.
//     A flat row has NO subDepartments key — that belongs to the tree shape.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 02  THE TREE                                            -> 200 OK
//     ?tree=true
//     OUT: roots, totalElements (every unit at any depth, NOT the number of
//     roots), liftedToTop and depth. A leaf still has subDepartments: [].
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 03  A TREE CANNOT BE PAGED                              -> 400 Bad Request
//     ?tree=true&page=0, and ?tree=true&size=10.
//     OUT: { "code": "TREE_CANNOT_BE_PAGED" } — refused, not ignored.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 04  THE ORPHAN CASE                                     -> 200 OK
//     Retire a PARENT whose child is still active, then ?tree=true&active=true.
//     The parent is gone; the child is at the TOP with liftedToTop: true and
//     still names the parent it belongs to. It did not vanish.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 05  A RETIRED UNIT KEEPS ITS PLACE                      -> 200 OK
//     ?tree=true with no active filter. Still in the tree, marked
//     active:false — a tree with a hole in the middle is not a tree.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 06  SEARCH BY CODE                                      -> 200 OK
//     ?search= a code whose unit name shares nothing with it.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 07  SEARCH BY NAME                                      -> 200 OK
//     ?search=scien — case-insensitive, matches anywhere.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 08  A STRAY REGEX CHARACTER                             -> 200 OK
//     ?search=Sci( — an empty page, not a 500.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 09  THE CHILDREN OF ONE UNIT                            -> 200 OK
//     ?parentDepartmentDocsId={{departmentDocsId}}
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 10  WHAT ONE PERSON RUNS                                -> 200 OK
//     ?headStaffDocsId= a real Staff.id.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 11  THE ROOTS ONLY                                      -> 200 OK
//     ?topLevelOnly=true, then false for everything nested. Asked with
//     exists, so a unit written before the field existed reads as top-level.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 12  ACTIVE OR RETIRED                                   -> 200 OK
//     ?active=true, then false, then leave it off for BOTH.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 13  FILTERS COMBINE                                     -> 200 OK
//     ?active=true&topLevelOnly=true
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 14  PAGING THE FLAT LIST                                -> 200 OK
//     ?page=0&size=2, then page 1, then a page past the end (empty, not an
//     error). totalElements counts every match, not the page.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 15  THE TIEBREAKER                                      -> 200 OK
//     Create two units both named "Science", then ?sort=name. They come back
//     in departmentCode order — a department name is NOT unique.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 16  A SCHOOL WITH NOTHING                               -> 200 OK
//     ?tree=true on an empty school: roots: [], depth: 0. Never a 404.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 17  A SUSPENDED SCHOOL                                  -> 200 OK
//     No gate runs on a read.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
//  EVERY REFUSAL
//     400 TREE_CANNOT_BE_PAGED             tree=true sent with page or size.
//     400 INVALID_PAGE                     page is negative.
//     400 INVALID_PAGE_SIZE                size is below 1 or above 100.
//     400 INVALID_SORT_FIELD               A sort field not on the allowlist.
//     400 TENANT_NOT_RESOLVED              The X-School-Subdomain header is missing or blank.
//     404 SCHOOL_NOT_FOUND                 No school has that subdomain.

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  PATCH /schools/current/departments/{id}
// Every field optional. Needs X-School-Subdomain and a department id.
//
//  ABSENT MEANS LEAVE IT ALONE, and an empty body is 400 NOTHING_TO_UPDATE
//  rather than a no-op 200 — a PATCH that changes nothing and answers success
//  lets a client with a broken form look healthy.
//
//  NEVER departmentCode. Nothing joins on it, which is exactly what makes
//  editing it dangerous: no query would break, and every export, filter and
//  report naming the old code would quietly stop matching.
//
//  NEVER THE PARENT — A UNIT CANNOT BE MOVED. The plan had #10 moving one and
//  refusing a cycle at 409 DEPARTMENT_CYCLE; dropped 2026-09-15. Nothing in
//  this API can write a cycle into the department chart any more.
//
//  active IS HERE RATHER THAN ON #11's ENDPOINT PAIR, and it carries #11's
//  refusal with it: retiring a unit that still holds ACTIVE seats is a 409
//  DEPARTMENT_NOT_EMPTY naming how many. Sub-departments do NOT block it —
//  #12 lifts them and marks liftedToTop. Restoring has no check.
//
//  "" CLEARS description and headStaffDocsId. "" on name is refused.
// =========================================================================
//
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 01  A RENAME                                            -> 200 OK
//     { "name": "Teaching & Learning" }
//     OUT: the new name, the code untouched.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 02  NOTHING AT ALL                                      -> 400 Bad Request
//     {}   OUT: { "code": "NOTHING_TO_UPDATE" } — not a quiet 200.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 03  ONLY UNEDITABLE FIELDS                              -> 400 Bad Request
//     { "departmentCode": "NEWCODE", "parentDepartmentDocsId": "..." }
//     The same 400: neither is on the request record, so the request is
//     empty. Both are IGNORED on the way in, never refused.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 04  THE NAME CANNOT BE REMOVED                          -> 400 Bad Request
//     { "name": "   " }   OUT: { "code": "DEPARTMENT_NAME_REQUIRED" }
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 05  CLEARING THE DESCRIPTION                            -> 200 OK
//     { "description": "" }
//     OUT: no description key at all — absent, not null or "".
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 06  CLEARING THE HEAD                                   -> 200 OK
//     { "headStaffDocsId": "" }
//     OUT: no headStaffDocsId key. The unit has no named head.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 07  AN UNKNOWN HEAD                                     -> 404 Not Found
//     { "name": "Renamed", "headStaffDocsId": "deadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeef" }
//     OUT: { "code": "STAFF_NOT_FOUND" } — and the NAME does not land
//     either. The whole write is rejected.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 08  RETIRING AN EMPTY UNIT                              -> 200 OK
//     { "active": false }
//     OUT: active false, and a nextStep saying it keeps its place in the tree.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 09  RETIRING ONE THAT STILL HOLDS SEATS                 -> 409 Conflict
//     Create two seats in it first, then { "active": false }.
//     OUT: { "code": "DEPARTMENT_NOT_EMPTY" } and "2 seats are still
//     active" — the count is in the message because "retire the two seats
//     first" is actionable and "not empty" is not.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 10  RETIRING A PARENT WHOSE CHILDREN ARE ACTIVE         -> 200 OK
//     Allowed, and not an oversight: #12 lifts those children to the top and
//     marks liftedToTop. That state is designed for; a live SEAT is not.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 11  RESTORING                                           -> 200 OK
//     { "active": true } — no check at all, even with active seats under it.
//     Putting a unit back cannot invalidate anything.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 12  ANOTHER SCHOOL'S UNIT                               -> 404 Not Found
//     A REAL department id belonging to a different school.
//     OUT: { "code": "DEPARTMENT_NOT_FOUND" } — the lookup carries schoolId.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
//  EVERY REFUSAL
//     400 NOTHING_TO_UPDATE                No editable field was sent.
//     400 DEPARTMENT_NAME_REQUIRED         name sent blank.
//     400 TENANT_NOT_RESOLVED              The X-School-Subdomain header is missing or blank.
//     403 SCHOOL_NOT_ACTIVE                Gate 1 — suspended or closed. Reads still work.
//     404 SCHOOL_NOT_FOUND                 No school has that subdomain.
//     404 DEPARTMENT_NOT_FOUND             Not a department of this school.
//     404 STAFF_NOT_FOUND                  headStaffDocsId names nobody here.
//     409 DEPARTMENT_NOT_EMPTY             active:false while seats are active.

{
    "name": "Teaching & Learning"
}

