// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  GET /schools/current/positions
// A GET — no body. Needs X-School-Subdomain.
//
//  THE FILLED COUNT IS THE ENDPOINT. Everything else on the row is already
//  on #52. filledHeadcount is counted from CURRENT employment records on
//  every call and NEVER STORED — a counter on the position document drifts
//  the first time a writer forgets it.
//
//  ONE GROUPED COUNT FOR THE PAGE, not one per row. Twenty seats answered by
//  twenty countBy... calls is the N+1 that makes a list slower the more it
//  returns.
//
//  vacancies NEVER GOES BELOW ZERO. #16 warns rather than refusing when a
//  school over-hires, so filled can exceed approved — and a negative would
//  read as a seat owing people. The overflow is overFilled: true instead.
//
//  ?vacant= CANNOT BE APPLIED BEFORE PAGING. Vacancy is not a field, so that
//  path reads the whole matching set, counts it, filters, and pages in
//  memory. Every other call counts only the page.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  TWO OF THREE FILLED               -> 200  filledHeadcount 2, vacancies 1,
//                                              overFilled false.
// 02  A SEAT NOBODY HOLDS               -> 200  filledHeadcount 0 — PRESENT,
//                                              not omitted. The aggregation
//                                              cannot bucket what it did not
//                                              match; the service fills it.
// 03  OVER-FILLED                       -> 200  approved 1, two people.
//                                              vacancies 0 (floored),
//                                              overFilled true.
// 04  EXACTLY FULL IS NOT OVER-FILLED   -> 200  approved 1, one person.
//                                              overFilled FALSE — the boundary
//                                              > and >= disagree on.
// 05  ONLY CURRENT RECORDS COUNT        -> 200  employ, then employ elsewhere.
//                                              The seat they LEFT drops to 0.
// 06  ?vacant=true                      -> 200  only seats with room.
// 07  ?vacant=false IS NOT 'FULL'       -> 200  the full seat AND the
//                                              over-filled one.
// 08  A VACANT PAGE IS FULL, NOT SHORT  -> 200  ?vacant=true&size=2 returns
//                                              exactly 2, and totalElements
//                                              counts the VACANT set.
// 09  A PAGE PAST THE END               -> 200  content [] — not a 500.
// 10  NO teachingPosition KEY           -> 200  answers ?teaching=false,
//                                              absent from ?teaching=true.
// 11  AN UNBALANCED BRACKET             -> 200  ?search=Teacher( is empty, not
//                                              a 500 from PatternSyntaxException.
// 12  ?sort=filledHeadcount             -> 400  INVALID_SORT_FIELD — computed
//                                              after the page is chosen.
// 13  ANOTHER SCHOOL'S SEATS            -> 200  absent, and the COUNT is scoped
//                                              too.
// 14  A SUSPENDED SCHOOL                -> 200  no gate runs on a read.
//
//  EVERY REFUSAL
//     400 TENANT_NOT_RESOLVED              The X-School-Subdomain header is missing or blank.
//     400 INVALID_SORT_FIELD               ?sort= named a field off the allowlist.
//     400 INVALID_PAGE_SIZE                ?size= above 100 or below 1.
//     404 SCHOOL_NOT_FOUND                 No school has that subdomain.

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  GET /schools/current/positions/{id}
// A GET — no body. Needs X-School-Subdomain and a POSITION id.
//
//  NOT IN THE ORIGINAL PLAN, the way #52 was not. #15 answers "3 of 5 filled"
//  and a school immediately asks WHICH THREE. Answering that from the
//  numbered endpoints means #7, which has no employment filter yet.
//
//  THE COUNT AND THE LIST COME FROM ONE READ. filledHeadcount is
//  holders.length, not a second count query: two reads of the same collection
//  a moment apart can disagree, and a page showing "3 filled" above two names
//  is a bug report nobody can reproduce.
//
//  CURRENT HOLDERS ONLY — a seat is not a history. A closed record names
//  somebody who USED TO hold this. One person's history is #19.
//
//  LONGEST-SERVING FIRST, the opposite of #19's order. A history is read
//  newest-first because the current row is the interesting one; a roster
//  oldest-first because seniority is what distinguishes otherwise identical
//  rows.
//
//  A HOLDER WHOSE PERSON IS MISSING IS MARKED, NEVER DROPPED. Dropping it
//  would make the seat look less filled than it is, and then the count and
//  the list would disagree.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  A SEAT WITH TWO PEOPLE IN IT      -> 200  holders, longest-serving first.
// 02  THE COUNT EQUALS THE LIST         -> 200  filledHeadcount === holders.length,
//                                              ALWAYS.
// 03  A HOLDER CARRIES BOTH IDS         -> 200  staffDocsId addresses the PERSON
//                                              (#2, #8); employmentDocsId the
//                                              POSTING (#18).
// 04  AND NOTHING SENSITIVE             -> 200  no dateOfBirth, no address, no
//                                              emergency contact. There is no
//                                              authorization here.
// 05  A SEAT NOBODY HOLDS               -> 200  holders [], and a holdersNote
//                                              saying that is a REAL state.
// 06  CURRENT HOLDERS ONLY              -> 200  employ, then employ elsewhere:
//                                              the seat they left is empty.
// 07  A RETIRED SEAT WITH PEOPLE IN IT  -> 200  reachable, because #14 does not
//                                              check the count before retiring —
//                                              POSITION_STILL_FILLED is owed.
// 08  A HOLDER WHOSE PERSON WAS DELETED -> 200  the posting is STILL returned,
//                                              with no fullName and a note.
// 09  A RECORD NAMING ANOTHER SCHOOL'S
//     PERSON                            -> 200  counted, but their NAME is not
//                                              returned — the staff lookup
//                                              carries schoolId.
// 10  THE UNIT AND LINE ARE RESOLVED    -> 200  departmentName and
//                                              reportsToPositionTitle. A seat
//                                              reporting to nobody carries
//                                              NEITHER field.
// 11  AN UNKNOWN SEAT                   -> 404  POSITION_NOT_FOUND.
// 12  ANOTHER SCHOOL'S SEAT             -> 404  POSITION_NOT_FOUND.
// 13  A SUSPENDED SCHOOL                -> 200  no gate runs on a read.
//
//  EVERY REFUSAL
//     400 TENANT_NOT_RESOLVED              The X-School-Subdomain header is missing or blank.
//     404 SCHOOL_NOT_FOUND                 No school has that subdomain.
//     404 POSITION_NOT_FOUND               Not a position of this school.

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  GET /schools/current/admission-cycles
//  Run Session / Sign in first. A GET has no body; the cases are the query
//  parameters below. Enable and disable them in the Params tab.
//
//  EVERY FILTER IS OPTIONAL. Send none and you get the school's rounds,
//  newest year first then by name. That pair is unique within a school, so
//  the order is total and paging cannot show a row twice.
//
//  NO YEAR IS REQUIRED, which is the opposite of classes and terms. A school
//  works on two years at once during admissions, so "show me both" is the
//  starting point rather than something to ask for.
//
//  NO GATES RUN. A suspended school still lists the rounds it ran.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  EVERYTHING                                           -> 200 OK
//     All params disabled except page and size.
//
// 02  ONE YEAR            ?academicYear=2026-2027          -> 200 OK
//     A year with nothing in it is an EMPTY PAGE, never a 404 — there is no
//     year in the path to be wrong about.
//
// 03  THE ROUNDS NOBODY OPENED YET   ?status=DRAFT         -> 200 OK
//     Everything Create makes starts here; #3 is not built to move it.
//
// 04  SEARCH THE NAME     ?search=main                     -> 200 OK
//     Matches anywhere in the name and ignores case. Try MAIN and MaIn too.
//
// 05  A REGEX METACHARACTER   ?search=(                    -> 200 OK
//     An unbalanced bracket. The needle is quoted before it is compiled, so
//     this is an empty result rather than a 500.
//
// 06  OPEN ON A DAY   ?openOn=2026-07-15T00:00:00Z         -> 200 OK
//     Rounds whose application window covered that moment. A cycle missing
//     either date NEVER matches: it is not open forever, its calendar was
//     never filled in.
//
// 07  A FIELD NOT ON THE ALLOWLIST   ?sort=schoolId  -> 400 INVALID_SORT_FIELD
//     The message lists what IS allowed. Try ?sort=notes as well.
//     Ordering is a read, which is why the allowlist is a control and not a
//     convenience: sort by a field and walk the pages and you learn its
//     values even when nothing displays them.
//
// 08  PAGE ONE AT A TIME   ?size=1&page=0, then page=1 ... -> 200 OK
//     No row appears twice and none is skipped, with or without a sort.
//     A page past the end is an empty page, not a 404.
//
// 09  SIZE OVER THE CAP    ?size=101           -> 400 INVALID_PAGE_SIZE
//
// 10  A NEGATIVE PAGE      ?page=-1                 -> 400 INVALID_PAGE
//
// 11  A SUSPENDED SCHOOL STILL READS                       -> 200 OK
//     Sign in as a SUSPENDED school. This answers 200 and Create Admission
//     Cycle answers 409 SCHOOL_NOT_EDITABLE. Reads run no gates.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  GET /schools/current/admission-cycles/{id}
//  Run Session / Sign in, then Create Admission Cycle — it saves the id
//  into {{admissionCycleDocsId}}.
//
//  WHAT THIS ADDS OVER A ROW OF #5: the notes, and the seat table itself
//  rather than a count of it, plus totalSeats added up server-side.
//
//  EACH SEAT ROW CARRIES ITS CLASS'S NAME, resolved in one query for all of
//  them. A class that is GONE still gets a row, with no name — a cycle
//  holding seats for a class the school no longer has is a real problem and
//  hiding it would be the wrong kind of tidy.
//
//  IT DOES NOT SAY HOW THE SEATS ARE DOING. Offered, accepted, enrolled and
//  free are counted from the applications and that is #7, not built.
//
//  NO GATES. A suspended school still opens the rounds it ran.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  OPEN A CYCLE                                         -> 200 OK
//     OUT: notes and capacities, neither of which is on a #5 row.
//
// 02  A CYCLE WITH NO SEATS                                -> 200 OK
//     capacities: [], capacityCount 0, totalSeats 0. Normal, not a refusal:
//     #4 sets the seat table and is not built, so every cycle reads back
//     this way today.
//
// 03  AN ID THAT IS NOT THERE      -> 404 ADMISSION_CYCLE_NOT_FOUND
//     Change one character of the id.
//
// 04  ANOTHER SCHOOL'S REAL ID     -> 404 ADMISSION_CYCLE_NOT_FOUND
//     THE ONE WORTH RUNNING. Sign in as a different school and ask for this
//     cycle. It answers 404 and never the cycle — the school is part of the
//     lookup rather than something checked afterwards.
//
// 05  A MALFORMED ID                              -> 4xx, never a 500
//     Put "not-an-object-id" in the path.
//
// 06  A SUSPENDED SCHOOL STILL READS                       -> 200 OK
//     Or 404 for an unknown id — either way NOT 409. Reads run no gates,
//     while Create Admission Cycle still answers 409 SCHOOL_NOT_EDITABLE.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------

{
  "name": "Main intake (revised)"
}

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  PATCH /schools/current/admission-cycles/{id}
//  Run Session / Sign in, then Create Admission Cycle.
//
//  ONLY WHAT YOU SEND MOVES. An absent field is left alone. A body that
//  changes nothing is 400 NOTHING_TO_UPDATE, never a silent 200 — a no-op
//  that answers 200 looks exactly like a change that worked.
//
//  CLEARING NEEDS ITS OWN LIST, and this is the first endpoint where that
//  is true. "" clears a String, but there is no empty Instant and a record
//  cannot tell an absent key from a null one — both arrive as null. So
//  "clear": ["applicationCloseAt"] is the only way to remove a date.
//
//  THE DATES ARE CHECKED AS THEY WILL END UP, merged with what is stored.
//  Case 04 is the one that proves it.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  RENAME IT                                            -> 200 OK
//     The body above. Every date and the notes stay exactly as they were.
//
// 02  A BODY THAT CHANGES NOTHING           -> 400 NOTHING_TO_UPDATE
// {}
//     Or send the name it already has — same answer.
//
// 03  CLEAR A DATE                                         -> 200 OK
//     The only way to remove one. Clearing an already-empty date is
//     NOTHING_TO_UPDATE, because it changes nothing.
// {
//   "clear": ["applicationCloseAt"]
// }
//
// 04  A DATE WRONG AGAINST WHAT IS STORED
//                                     -> 400 CYCLE_DATES_OUT_OF_ORDER
//     THE ONE WORTH RUNNING. Create a cycle with only an applicationOpenAt
//     of 2026-07-01, then send this. The close date is fine on its own and
//     wrong against the stored open date — only the merged pair can tell.
// {
//   "applicationCloseAt": "2026-06-01T00:00:00Z"
// }
//
// 05  SET AND CLEAR THE SAME FIELD  -> 400 CLEAR_CONFLICTS_WITH_VALUE
// {
//   "applicationCloseAt": "2026-09-01T00:00:00Z",
//   "clear": ["applicationCloseAt"]
// }
//
// 06  A MISSPELLED CLEAR FIELD          -> 400 UNKNOWN_CLEAR_FIELD
//     Refused, never ignored: a caller who typos this should be told, not
//     left believing a date was removed.
// {
//   "clear": ["applicationClosedAt"]
// }
//
// 07  BLANK THE NAME                        -> 400 BLANK_CYCLE_NAME
//     A cycle needs one. "" is a refusal, not a clear.
// {
//   "name": ""
// }
//
// 08  A NAME ANOTHER ROUND HOLDS              -> 409 CYCLE_NAME_TAKEN
// {
//   "name": "Scholarship round"
// }
//
// 09  TRY TO MOVE IT TO ANOTHER YEAR      -> 400 NOTHING_TO_UPDATE
//     academicYear is not accepted — ignored rather than refused, the
//     ordinary shape for a field the request record does not declare.
//     Read it back with Get: the year has not moved.
// {
//   "academicYear": "2027-2028"
// }
//
// 10  A STALE VERSION                 -> 409 CONCURRENT_MODIFICATION
//     Send this twice. The second is refused and does NOT land.
// {
//   "name": "Renamed again",
//   "version": 0
// }
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------

{
  "capacities": [
    { "classDocsId": "{{schoolClassId}}", "totalSeats": 60, "reservedSeats": 10 }
  ]
}

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  PUT /admission-cycles/{id}/capacities
//  Run Sign in, Create Academic Year, Create Class, then Create Admission
//  Cycle — and make sure the cycle's year is the class's year.
//
//  A PUT, AND IT REPLACES. Whoever sets intake reads the whole table and
//  rewrites it. A shorter list REMOVES the rows you left out — sending one
//  row sets the table to one row, it does not add one.
//
//  A per-row PATCH was not possible: IntakeCapacity is embedded and has no
//  id. The class is all that identifies a row.
//
//  EVERY CLASS MUST BE IN THE CYCLE'S YEAR, not merely in this school. A
//  cycle admits into one year, so seats against another year's class would
//  be seats nobody could ever fill. Case 05 is the one worth running.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  SET THE SEATS                                        -> 200 OK
//     The body above. OUT: the whole cycle, className resolved per row.
//
// 02  IT REPLACES — send fewer rows                        -> 200 OK
//     Set two classes, then send one. The other is GONE, not merged.
//
// 03  CLEAR THE TABLE                                      -> 200 OK
// {
//   "capacities": []
// }
//
// 04  FORGET THE FIELD ENTIRELY               -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
//     NOT the same as case 03. Forgetting to send the table and
//     deliberately emptying it must not be one request.
// {}
//
// 05  A CLASS FROM ANOTHER YEAR         -> 409 CLASS_NOT_IN_CYCLE_YEAR
//     Use a REAL class of this school that belongs to a different year.
//     Scoping by school alone would accept it, and the seats would be
//     against a class the cycle could never admit into.
//
// 06  THE SAME CLASS TWICE             -> 409 DUPLICATE_CAPACITY_CLASS
// {
//   "capacities": [
//     { "classDocsId": "{{schoolClassId}}", "totalSeats": 10 },
//     { "classDocsId": "{{schoolClassId}}", "totalSeats": 20 }
//   ]
// }
//
// 07  RESERVE MORE THAN EXIST            -> 400 RESERVED_EXCEEDS_TOTAL
// {
//   "capacities": [
//     { "classDocsId": "{{schoolClassId}}", "totalSeats": 10, "reservedSeats": 11 }
//   ]
// }
//
// 08  RESERVE ALL OF THEM                                  -> 200 OK
//     The boundary, not past it.
// {
//   "capacities": [
//     { "classDocsId": "{{schoolClassId}}", "totalSeats": 10, "reservedSeats": 10 }
//   ]
// }
//
// 09  ZERO SEATS                                           -> 200 OK
//     A row, not an omission — "this class is offering none".
// {
//   "capacities": [
//     { "classDocsId": "{{schoolClassId}}", "totalSeats": 0 }
//   ]
// }
//
// 10  ONE BAD ROW AMONG GOOD ONES                          -> 409
//     The WHOLE table is refused. Read it back with Get — not even the
//     good row was written.
// {
//   "capacities": [
//     { "classDocsId": "{{schoolClassId}}", "totalSeats": 10 },
//     { "classDocsId": "6aa39612224c2e933a1cFFFF", "totalSeats": 10 }
//   ]
// }
//
// 11  A STALE VERSION                 -> 409 CONCURRENT_MODIFICATION
//     Matters more here than on a correction: this write REPLACES, so the
//     loser silently loses every row the winner added.
// {
//   "version": 0,
//   "capacities": [
//     { "classDocsId": "{{schoolClassId}}", "totalSeats": 5 }
//   ]
// }
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------

{
  "status": "OPEN"
}

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  POST /admission-cycles/{id}/status
//  Run Sign in, Create Admission Cycle, then Set Admission Cycle Seats.
//
//  THE ENDPOINT THE REST OF THE MODULE WAITED FOR. An application can only
//  go into a cycle that is OPEN — CYCLE_NOT_OPEN, this module's replacement
//  for gate 4 — and until #3 existed no cycle could leave DRAFT.
//
//      DRAFT ──> SCHEDULED ──> OPEN ──> CLOSED ──> COMPLETED
//        │           │           │         │
//        └───────────┴───────────┴─────────┴──> CANCELLED
//
//  IT ONLY GOES FORWARDS. COMPLETED and CANCELLED are both terminal, and a
//  cycle closed by mistake cannot be reopened — the safe undo is a new
//  cycle, which costs a name.
//
//  OPENING NEEDS A SEAT TABLE. Not an invented rule: #17 refuses an
//  application whose class is not in the cycle's capacities, so an OPEN
//  cycle with an empty table is a round nobody can apply to.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  OPEN IT                                              -> 200 OK
//     The body above. Set the seats first, or case 02 happens.
//
// 02  OPEN WITH NO SEATS                  -> 409 CYCLE_HAS_NO_SEATS
//     THE ONE WORTH RUNNING. Create a cycle, do NOT set seats, send this.
//
// 03  THE WHOLE PATH                                 -> 200 OK each
//     SCHEDULED, then OPEN, then CLOSED, then COMPLETED. Four calls.
// { "status": "SCHEDULED" }
//
// 04  TRY TO REOPEN A CLOSED ROUND -> 409 INVALID_CYCLE_TRANSITION
//     The refusal lists what IS reachable: COMPLETED and CANCELLED.
// { "status": "OPEN" }
//
// 05  SKIP THE MIDDLE              -> 409 INVALID_CYCLE_TRANSITION
//     DRAFT straight to COMPLETED is not a move.
// { "status": "COMPLETED" }
//
// 06  ASK FOR WHERE IT ALREADY IS  -> 409 INVALID_CYCLE_TRANSITION
//     A silent 200 would tell you that you opened a cycle you did not.
//
// 07  CANCEL IT                                            -> 200 OK
//     Reachable from DRAFT, SCHEDULED, OPEN and CLOSED. Terminal.
// { "status": "CANCELLED" }
//
// 08  MOVE A CANCELLED ROUND       -> 409 INVALID_CYCLE_TRANSITION
//     Terminal means NOTHING is reachable — try every status.
// { "status": "DRAFT" }
//
// 09  A STALE VERSION               -> 409 CONCURRENT_MODIFICATION
// { "status": "OPEN", "version": 0 }
//
// 10  AND NOW #5 CAN FILTER BY IT                          -> 200 OK
//     List Admission Cycles with ?status=OPEN. Before #3 that filter could
//     only ever return DRAFT rows, because nothing could move.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------

{
  "academicYear": "{{academicYearName}}",
  "name": "Main intake"
}

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  POST /schools/current/admission-cycles
//  Run Sign in first. Needs an academic year that exists.
//
//  THE YEAR DOES NOT HAVE TO BE THE RUNNING ONE, and that is the whole point
//  of this module. Every other module refuses a write against a year the
//  school is not running; a school sets up its 2027-2028 admissions in the
//  middle of 2026-2027, and often has two cycles live at once. So gate 4 is
//  not run here. Case 02 is the one that proves it.
//
//  THERE IS NO YEAR IN THE PATH either, unlike classes and timetables. For
//  those the year is the scope. Here it is a field on the cycle.
//
//  SEATS ARE NOT ACCEPTED HERE. The cycle is created as a DRAFT with none,
//  and the seat table is #4. A create that could fail on either a duplicate
//  name or a bad seat row leaves the caller working out which.
//
//  THE NAME IS UNIQUE PER YEAR, NOT PER SCHOOL. "Main intake" in 2026-2027
//  and "Main intake" in 2027-2028 are two different cycles, both allowed.
// =========================================================================
//
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 01  CREATE A CYCLE                                      -> 201 Created
//     The body above.
//     OUT: admissionCycleId, status: "DRAFT", capacityCount: 0, nextStep
//     Header: Location: /schools/current/admission-cycles/{id}
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// 02  A YEAR THE SCHOOL IS NOT RUNNING                    -> 201 Created
//     The same call against a year whose isThisYearRunning is false. Creating
//     a CLASS for that year answers 409 ACADEMIC_YEAR_NOT_RUNNING; this
//     answers 201. That difference is the module's reason to exist.
// {
//   "academicYear": "2027-2028",
//   "name": "Next year main intake"
// }
//
// 03  WITH ALL FOUR DATES                                 -> 201 Created
//     They have to run forwards: enquiries open, applications open,
//     applications close, then the enrollment deadline.
// {
//   "academicYear": "{{academicYearName}}",
//   "name": "Dated intake",
//   "inquiryOpenAt": "2026-10-01T00:00:00Z",
//   "applicationOpenAt": "2026-11-01T00:00:00Z",
//   "applicationCloseAt": "2027-01-31T18:29:59Z",
//   "enrollmentDeadlineAt": "2027-03-15T18:29:59Z",
//   "notes": "Board intake for the main campus."
// }
//
// 04  ONLY SOME OF THE DATES                              -> 201 Created
//     All four are optional. Only the ones sent are compared, so a school can
//     give the application window now and fill the rest in later.
// {
//   "academicYear": "{{academicYearName}}",
//   "name": "Half dated intake",
//   "applicationOpenAt": "2026-11-01T00:00:00Z",
//   "applicationCloseAt": "2027-01-31T18:29:59Z"
// }
//
// 05  DATES IN THE WRONG ORDER            -> 400 CYCLE_DATES_OUT_OF_ORDER
//     Applications close before they open. The message names both dates in
//     words and shows them the way a person reads a date.
// {
//   "academicYear": "{{academicYearName}}",
//   "name": "Backwards intake",
//   "applicationOpenAt": "2027-02-01T00:00:00Z",
//   "applicationCloseAt": "2027-01-01T00:00:00Z"
// }
//
// 06  THE SAME NAME TWICE IN ONE YEAR            -> 409 CYCLE_NAME_TAKEN
//     Send case 01 again. The message names the year and the cycle.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// 07  THE SAME NAME IN A DIFFERENT YEAR                   -> 201 Created
//     Allowed. The name only has to be free inside its own year.
// {
//   "academicYear": "2027-2028",
//   "name": "Main intake"
// }
//
// 08  A YEAR THAT DOES NOT EXIST            -> 404 ACADEMIC_YEAR_NOT_FOUND
// {
//   "academicYear": "1999-2000",
//   "name": "Ghost intake"
// }
//
// 09  NO NAME                                            -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
// {
//   "academicYear": "{{academicYearName}}"
// }
//
// 10  NO YEAR                                            -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
// {
//   "name": "Yearless intake"
// }
//
// 11  WITHOUT SIGNING IN FIRST               -> 400 TENANT_NOT_RESOLVED
//     Run Sign in case 03 to clear the cookie, then send case 01.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------

{
  "admissionCycleDocsId": "{{admissionCycleDocsId}}",
  "appliedClassDocsId": "{{schoolClassId}}",
  "applicantName": "Aarav Sharma",
  "dateOfBirth": "2020-04-11",
  "gender": "MALE",
  "guardians": [
    {
      "fullName": "Rohan Sharma",
      "relation": "FATHER",
      "phoneNumber": "+919876543210",
      "primaryContact": true
    }
  ]
}

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  POST /schools/current/applications
//  Run Sign in, Create Class, Create Admission Cycle, Set Seats, then
//  Move Status to OPEN. An application needs all of that.
//
//  THE CYCLE MUST BE OPEN. This is the module's replacement for gate 4:
//  every other module asks "is this the running year"; admissions cannot,
//  because a cycle for next year is the normal case, so it asks the CYCLE.
//
//  THE INQUIRY IS OPTIONAL, and that is the point — the family that walks
//  in with a completed form never enquired. It is also why the pipeline is
//  testable without a single lead in the database.
//
//  #8, the endpoint that captures a lead, IS NOT BUILT. Nothing can create
//  an inquiry through the API yet, so cases 05 to 07 need a row put in
//  directly.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  A WALK-IN, NO INQUIRY                              -> 201 Created
//     The body above. OUT: status DRAFT, a generated applicationNo,
//     and appliedClassName resolved.
//
// 02  INTO A CYCLE THAT IS NOT OPEN            -> 409 CYCLE_NOT_OPEN
//     THE ONE WORTH RUNNING. Use a DRAFT cycle. There is no "is the year
//     running" check anywhere in this module — this is what replaced it.
//
// 03  A CLASS WITH NO SEATS              -> 409 CLASS_NOT_IN_CAPACITY
//     A class of the cycle's year that is NOT in its seat table. It could
//     never be offered anything.
//
// 04  A CLASS FROM ANOTHER YEAR         -> 409 CLASS_NOT_IN_CYCLE_YEAR
//     A different refusal from case 03, and worth telling apart.
//
// 05  FROM AN INQUIRY                                   -> 201 Created
//     Put a real inquiry id in. The lead moves to APPLICATION_STARTED.
//
// 06  THE SAME INQUIRY TWICE IN ONE CYCLE
//                                    -> 409 APPLICATION_ALREADY_EXISTS
//     One inquiry is one child applying once per round — an Inquiry carries
//     the child's own name and date of birth. A second child needs their
//     own inquiry. The SAME inquiry in a DIFFERENT cycle is allowed.
//
// 07  ANOTHER SCHOOL'S INQUIRY              -> 404 INQUIRY_NOT_FOUND
//     A real id belonging to a different school. The lookup carries the
//     school rather than checking it afterwards.
//
// 08  NO GUARDIANS                        -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
//     An inquiry may have none; an application may not. Send "guardians": []
//
// 09  A DATE OF BIRTH IN THE FUTURE       -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
//
// 10  WITH FORM ANSWERS                                 -> 201 Created
//     Stored exactly as sent — nothing validates them, because there is no
//     form definition to validate against. Over 200 keys is
//     400 TOO_MANY_FORM_ANSWERS, which is the only bound there can be.
// {
//   "admissionCycleDocsId": "{{admissionCycleDocsId}}",
//   "appliedClassDocsId": "{{schoolClassId}}",
//   "applicantName": "Aarav Sharma",
//   "dateOfBirth": "2020-04-11",
//   "gender": "MALE",
//   "guardians": [
//     { "fullName": "Rohan Sharma", "relation": "FATHER", "primaryContact": true }
//   ],
//   "formAnswers": { "previousSchool": "ABC School", "siblingsInSchool": 2 }
// }
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  GET /schools/current/applications
//  Run Session / Sign in first. A GET has no body; the cases are the query
//  parameters below. Enable and disable them in the Params tab.
//
//  THIS IS THE PIPELINE. Every form the school has, at whatever stage it
//  reached — a DRAFT nobody submitted sits beside an ENROLLED one.
//
//  EVERY FILTER IS OPTIONAL. Send none and you get the school's forms,
//  newest first then by application number. The number is unique within a
//  school, so the order is total and paging cannot show one row twice.
//
//  NO GATES RUN, and no cycle has to be open. A closed round's applications
//  are still read — refusing to show them would make the round unreviewable
//  the moment it stopped taking forms.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  EVERYTHING                                           -> 200 OK
//     All params disabled except page and size.
//
// 02  ONE ROUND      ?admissionCycleDocsId={{admissionCycleId}}  -> 200 OK
//     A cycle id from ANOTHER SCHOOL is an EMPTY PAGE, not a 404 and not a
//     leak: the school is added to the query, so the id simply matches
//     nothing. The filter is not a lookup and never confirms an id exists.
//
// 03  ONE CLASS      ?appliedClassDocsId={{schoolClassId}}       -> 200 OK
//     Cycle, then class, then status is the order of the index that serves
//     this — school_cycle_class_status_idx — and also the order an officer
//     narrows in.
//
// 04  ONE STAGE      ?status=DRAFT                              -> 200 OK
//     #17 creates in DRAFT and #19 is not built, so everything is DRAFT
//     today. Try SUBMITTED for the empty page that proves the filter runs.
//
// 05  A STATUS THAT IS NOT ONE   ?status=PENDING                -> 400
//     Spring refuses the value before the service is reached. The refusal
//     is the framework's, which is why it is not one of ours.
//
// 06  WHOSE WORKLIST
//       ?assignedAdmissionOfficerDocsId={{staffId}}            -> 200 OK
//     ALWAYS EMPTY TODAY. #22 assigns an officer and is not built, so no
//     application carries one. The filter is here so the field is testable
//     the day it is.
//
// 07  SEARCH         ?search=aarav                             -> 200 OK
//     The applicant's NAME or the application NUMBER, anywhere, ignoring
//     case. Try ?search=APP/2026/09 for the number side.
//
// 08  A REGEX METACHARACTER   ?search=(                        -> 200 OK
//     The needle is quoted before it is compiled, so an unbalanced bracket
//     is an empty result rather than a 500.
//
// 09  FROM A LEAD    ?fromInquiry=true                         -> 200 OK
//     Only forms that name an inquiry. ?fromInquiry=false gives the
//     walk-ins. Absent gives both.
//
//     NOTE the false side is `inquiryDocsId` MISSING, not null. A missing
//     field is not matched by $ne null in Mongo, which is why the query
//     asks by $exists rather than by inequality.
//
// 10  ORDER BY THE CHILD'S BIRTHDAY
//       ?sort=dateOfBirth                    -> 400 INVALID_SORT_FIELD
//     DELIBERATE. Sorting is a read: order by a date of birth and page
//     through, and you learn every applicant's age without a screen ever
//     showing one. Same reason guardians and formAnswers are off the list.
//     Allowed: applicationNo, applicantName, status, submittedAt,
//     createdAt, updatedAt.
//
// 11  ORDER BY WHEN IT WAS SUBMITTED   ?sort=submittedAt,desc  -> 200 OK
//     A DRAFT has no submittedAt. Those rows still come back — they sort
//     together, and the applicationNo tiebreaker decides them, which is
//     why submittedAt is not the default order.
//
// 12  A DIRECTION THAT IS NOT ONE
//       ?sort=createdAt,sideways       -> 400 INVALID_SORT_DIRECTION
//
// 13  PAGE ONE AT A TIME   ?size=1&page=0, then page=1 ...     -> 200 OK
//     No row appears twice and none is skipped, with or without a sort.
//     A page past the end is an empty page, not a 404.
//
// 14  SIZE OVER THE CAP    ?size=101              -> 400 INVALID_PAGE_SIZE
//
// 15  A NEGATIVE PAGE      ?page=-1                    -> 400 INVALID_PAGE
//
// 16  A SUSPENDED SCHOOL STILL READS                          -> 200 OK
//     Sign in as a SUSPENDED school. This answers 200 and Start an
//     Application answers 409 SCHOOL_NOT_EDITABLE. Reads run no gates.
//
// 17  ANOTHER SCHOOL'S PIPELINE IS NOT HERE                   -> 200 OK
//     Sign in as a different school. None of the rows above appear. The
//     school is added to every query in the repository, never taken from
//     anything the caller sent.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  GET /schools/current/applications/{admissionApplicationId}
//  Run Session / Sign in, then Start an Application — it saves the id.
//  A GET has no body; each case is a different id in the URL.
//
//  THIS IS THE FORM IN FULL. Everything a #24 row leaves off, plus the
//  REVIEWS and the OFFERS, which are not fields on the application at all
//  but rows in two other collections.
//
//  NO GATES. A suspended school still opens a form it already took.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  OPEN A FORM                                          -> 200 OK
//     OUT: guardians with their phone numbers, formAnswers, evidence ids,
//     admissionCycleName, academicYear and appliedClassName — none of which
//     are on a #24 row.
//
// 02  THE REVIEWS AND OFFERS ARE EMPTY                     -> 200 OK
//     reviews [], offers [], reviewCount 0, offerCount 0.
//
//     NOT A GAP. #26 assigns a reviewer, #27 records the result, #29 to #31
//     issue and answer and withdraw an offer — none are built. The queries
//     run and are scoped to your school; there is simply nothing to find.
//
//     When they exist: reviews come back OLDEST ROUND FIRST then by when
//     they were created (a round holds more than one — an interview and a
//     test), and offers come back FIRST REVISION FIRST with the superseded
//     ones still in. Showing only the live offer would make "what did we
//     originally offer this family" unanswerable.
//
// 03  A FORM WITH NO EXTRA ANSWERS                         -> 200 OK
//     formAnswers is LEFT OFF entirely rather than sent as {}. An absent
//     map and an empty one say the same thing, and one of them is noise.
//     evidenceDocumentDocsIds is [] though — a list that is there and empty
//     is a different thing from a field nobody set.
//
// 04  A GUARDIAN WHO GAVE NO PHONE NUMBER                  -> 200 OK
//     Start an Application with a second guardian carrying only fullName
//     and relation. The optional fields are absent on that guardian rather
//     than sent as empty strings.
//
// 05  THE PEOPLE ARE IDS, NOT NAMES                        -> 200 OK
//     assignedAdmissionOfficerDocsId is absent on every form today, and a
//     reviewer would be an id. #22 assigns an officer and #26 assigns a
//     reviewer; neither is built, so a name resolved here could never be
//     exercised. It gets written when the endpoint that fills it does.
//
// 06  nextStep SAYS WHAT CAN BE DONE                       -> 200 OK
//     A DRAFT names #19 and says it is not built, so nobody hunts for a
//     route that 404s. Every status answers differently.
//
// 07  AN ID THAT IS NOT THERE            -> 404 APPLICATION_NOT_FOUND
//     Change one character of the id.
//
// 08  ANOTHER SCHOOL'S REAL ID           -> 404 APPLICATION_NOT_FOUND
//     THE ONE WORTH RUNNING. Sign in as a different school and ask for
//     this application. It answers 404 and the body carries no name, no
//     date of birth and no phone number — the school is part of the query
//     rather than something checked after the read.
//
// 09  A MALFORMED ID                                 -> 404, never a 500
//     /not-an-object-id — a refusal, not a stack trace.
//
// 10  A TRAILING SLASH AND NOTHING ELSE               -> 404 NOT_FOUND
//     /applications/ is no route at all, so this is the framework's
//     refusal rather than one of ours — which is why the code is NOT_FOUND
//     and not APPLICATION_NOT_FOUND. It does NOT fall through to the list.
//
// 11  A SUSPENDED SCHOOL CAN STILL READ                    -> 200 OK
//     Reads run no gates. Start an Application on the same school still
//     answers 409 SCHOOL_NOT_EDITABLE, which is how you tell a read with
//     no gate from a read that has one.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  PATCH /schools/current/applications/{id}
//  Run Start an Application first — it saves admissionApplicationDocsId.
//
//  FAMILIES FILL A FORM OVER SEVERAL SITTINGS. Before this, Start an
//  Application created one and nothing could change it — a typo in a
//  child's name meant starting again.
//
//  DRAFT AND NOTHING ELSE. That is the line this module is built around:
//  after Submit an Application the applicant and guardian fields stop being
//  a draft and become a record of what the family actually declared.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  FIX A TYPO IN THE NAME                              -> 200 OK
//     Nothing else moves. The answers and the guardians are exactly where
//     they were — only what you send moves.
{
  "applicantName": "Aarav Sharma"
}
//
// 02  REPLACE THE GUARDIANS                               -> 200 OK
//     A LIST IS ONE VALUE. The ones already there are GONE: there is no id
//     on a guardian to merge by — they are embedded, not documents — and
//     merging would leave no way to remove one added by mistake.
// { "guardians": [{ "fullName": "Priya Sharma", "relation": "MOTHER", "primaryContact": true }] }
//
// 03  CLEAR THE ANSWERS                                   -> 200 OK
//     {} replaces the map with nothing. Leaving the field out is the other
//     thing entirely.
// { "formAnswers": {} }
//
// 04  CORRECT THE CLASS                                   -> 200 OK
//     Re-checked exactly as Start an Application checks it: a class of the
//     CYCLE'S year (409 CLASS_NOT_IN_CYCLE_YEAR) that the round has seats
//     set up for (409 CLASS_NOT_IN_CAPACITY).
// { "appliedClassDocsId": "{{schoolClassId}}" }
//
// 05  EDIT A SUBMITTED FORM      -> 409 APPLICATION_NOT_EDITABLE
//     THE ONE WORTH RUNNING. Submit it first. What the family declared is
//     the thing an admissions record is for, and a school that could
//     rewrite it afterwards could not answer what they actually told us.
//
// 06  A BODY THAT CHANGES NOTHING           -> 400 NOTHING_TO_UPDATE
//     ASKED FIRST, before the version and before the status. A version on
//     its own answers this too.
// {}
//
// 07  TRY TO MOVE THE CYCLE OR THE STATUS                 -> 200 OK
//     WORTH READING THE ANSWER. admissionCycleDocsId, inquiryDocsId and
//     status are IGNORED — only the name changes.
//
//     A form belongs to the round it was created against, which decides the
//     year, the seat table and the window Submit checks. Re-pointing the
//     inquiry would leave the old lead claiming a form it no longer has.
//     And DRAFT -> SUBMITTED is Submit an Application, which freezes the
//     snapshot as it goes.
// { "applicantName": "Still a draft", "admissionCycleDocsId": "6aa39612224c2e933a1cFFFF", "status": "SUBMITTED" }
//
// 08  A NAME SENT AS EMPTY            -> 400 BLANK_APPLICANT_NAME
//     Leaving the field out keeps the one it has. Sending "" is trying to
//     remove a name the document requires.
// { "applicantName": "   " }
//
// 09  NO GUARDIANS AT ALL                 -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
//     @Size(min = 1), NOT @NotEmpty — the difference is the whole of what a
//     PATCH means. @NotEmpty rejects null, which would have made guardians
//     required on every call: correcting a name would fail unless you
//     re-sent them. The suite found that on its first run.
// { "guardians": [] }
//
// 10  A BIRTHDAY IN THE FUTURE           -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
// { "dateOfBirth": "2099-01-01" }
//
// 11  MORE THAN 200 ANSWERS          -> 400 TOO_MANY_FORM_ANSWERS
//
// 12  A STALE VERSION                  -> 409 CONCURRENT_MODIFICATION
// { "applicantName": "Raced", "version": 0 }
//
// 13  ANOTHER SCHOOL'S APPLICATION        -> 404 APPLICATION_NOT_FOUND
//
// 14  A SUSPENDED SCHOOL                  -> 409 SCHOOL_NOT_EDITABLE
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  POST /schools/current/applications/{id}/submit
//  Run Session / Sign in, then Start an Application — it saves the id.
//  NO BODY. Everything this needs is already on the form.
//
//  THIS IS THE LINE THE MODULE IS BUILT AROUND. Before it the applicant and
//  guardian fields are a draft the family is still filling in. After it they
//  are a record of WHAT THE FAMILY ACTUALLY DECLARED, and #18 refuses to
//  edit them from here on.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  SEND A DRAFT                                         -> 200 OK
//     OUT: status SUBMITTED, submittedAt stamped, and a nextStep saying the
//     form is frozen. Everything else on the form is untouched.
//
// 02  SEND IT AGAIN            -> 409 INVALID_APPLICATION_TRANSITION
//     THE ONE WORTH RUNNING TWICE. The message says the form is ALREADY IN
//     rather than blaming the round, and submittedAt is NOT overwritten.
//
//     The DRAFT check runs BEFORE the cycle check, and that ordering is the
//     whole reason: somebody pressing submit twice on a round that has since
//     closed should be told about the form, not about the round.
//
// 03  A ROUND THAT CLOSED WHILE THE DRAFT SAT  -> 409 CYCLE_NOT_OPEN
//     Start a form, Move Admission Cycle Status to CLOSED, then submit.
//     THE MOMENT THAT COUNTS IS THE SUBMISSION, not when the draft began —
//     a form started an hour before the deadline and sent an hour after it
//     is a late application.
//
// 04  A ROUND NOBODY CLOSED                 -> 409 APPLICATIONS_CLOSED
//     Leave the cycle OPEN and PATCH applicationCloseAt into the past. The
//     status says nobody pressed a button; the date says what the school
//     promised families. Both are asked, because they catch different
//     mistakes.
//
// 05  A ROUND THAT HAS NOT STARTED    -> 409 APPLICATIONS_NOT_OPEN_YET
//     PATCH applicationOpenAt into the future on an OPEN cycle.
//
// 06  A FORM FROM A LEAD                                   -> 200 OK
//     The inquiry moves APPLICATION_STARTED -> APPLICATION_SUBMITTED. #17
//     is what moved it to APPLICATION_STARTED.
//
// 07  A FORM WHOSE LEAD WAS DELETED                        -> 200 OK
//     Still submits. #17 refuses an inquiry it cannot find, which is right
//     when the family is naming one — but here the link was checked when the
//     draft was started, and a lead somebody deleted since must not be able
//     to block the family. The form is what matters; the lead is a note
//     about how it arrived.
//
// 08  A CLASS TAKEN OUT OF THE SEAT TABLE                  -> 200 OK
//     DELIBERATE, and worth running. Set Admission Cycle Seats to a table
//     that excludes the applied class, then submit. It goes through:
//     submitting is the FAMILY'S act, and refusing it because the school
//     changed its own plan would punish the wrong side. Capacity is decided
//     when a seat is offered (#29) and counted by #7.
//
// 09  ANYTHING PAST DRAFT       -> 409 INVALID_APPLICATION_TRANSITION
//     WITHDRAWN, APPROVED, REJECTED, ENROLLED, OFFER_ACCEPTED. Nothing but
//     a DRAFT can be sent. Those messages do NOT say "already in" — that
//     wording is kept for a form that really is.
//
// 10  AN ID THAT IS NOT THERE            -> 404 APPLICATION_NOT_FOUND
//
// 11  ANOTHER SCHOOL'S FORM              -> 404 APPLICATION_NOT_FOUND
//     Sign in elsewhere. Never a 200, and the form stays a DRAFT.
//
//     CHECK THE CODE, not just the status. A school whose subscription has
//     lapsed answers 409 from the gate before it ever looks — which is a
//     different refusal, and reading "not a 200" as "tenant-scoped" is how
//     a missing scope hides.
//
// 12  A SUSPENDED SCHOOL                 -> 409 SCHOOL_NOT_EDITABLE
//     Refused by the gate BEFORE the form is looked up. That is how you tell
//     a write from a read here: #24 and #25 answer 200 for the same school.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------

{
    "reviewerDocsId": "{{staffDocsId}}",
    "reviewerRole": "ADMISSION_OFFICER",
    "reviewRound": 1,
    "dueAt": "2027-03-15T17:00:00Z",
    "notes": "Interview first, then the written test."
}

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  POST /schools/current/applications/{id}/reviews
//  Run Session / Sign in, Start an Application, then Submit an Application.
//  You also need a STAFF id of this school — People / Create Staff saves one.
//
//  IT ASSIGNS THE WORK; IT DOES NOT DO IT. The score, the criteria and the
//  recommendation are #27, which records the result and is not built. If one
//  call did both there would be no state in which a review is OUTSTANDING —
//  and that state is the whole of #28, a reviewer's queue.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  ASSIGN A REVIEWER                                 -> 201 Created
//     The body above. OUT: status PENDING, the reviewer NAMED, and the
//     application moved SUBMITTED -> UNDER_REVIEW.
//
// 02  A SECOND REVIEWER ON THE SAME ROUND               -> 201 Created
//     { "reviewerDocsId": "<somebody else>",
//       "reviewerRole": "SUBJECT_TEACHER" }
//     An interview and an entrance test are two reviews of round 1. The
//     application does NOT move again — it is already UNDER_REVIEW.
//
// 03  THE SAME PERSON TWICE       -> 409 REVIEWER_ALREADY_ASSIGNED
//     Send 01 again unchanged. The message names the person AND the round,
//     rather than being a duplicate-key error from
//     school_application_round_reviewer_uniq.
//
// 04  THE SAME PERSON, A DIFFERENT ROUND                -> 201 Created
//     { ..., "reviewRound": 2 }  Allowed: uniqueness is on the reviewer AND
//     the round. Round 2 opens because round 1 already EXISTS, not because
//     it was asked for.
//
// 04b A ROUND WITH NOTHING BEFORE IT
//                                -> 409 REVIEW_ROUND_OUT_OF_ORDER
//     { ..., "reviewRound": 5 } on a form with no reviews at all.
//     ROUNDS RUN 1, 2, 3 WITH NO GAPS. Round N needs round N-1 on that
//     application, by ANYBODY — a second assessor joining round 1 does not
//     open round 2, because the rounds are the school's stages rather than
//     one person's. A gap leaves a round that can never be filled in later.
//
// 05  A FORM NOBODY SENT           -> 409 APPLICATION_NOT_REVIEWABLE
//     Start an application and do NOT submit it. The message points at #19
//     rather than at the reviewer.
//
// 06  A FORM ALREADY DECIDED       -> 409 APPLICATION_NOT_REVIEWABLE
//     REJECTED, WITHDRAWN, OFFERED, OFFER_ACCEPTED, ENROLLED. A review
//     assigned after the decision is work nobody would read.
//
//     WAITLISTED and ADDITIONAL_INFORMATION_REQUIRED are ALLOWED — a school
//     holding an applicant for a seat often looks at them again when one
//     comes free. Neither is moved to UNDER_REVIEW: that is #20's move.
//
// 07  ANOTHER SCHOOL'S REAL STAFF ID       -> 404 STAFF_NOT_FOUND
//     THE ONE WORTH RUNNING. A ghost id proves nothing here — it is refused
//     with or without the tenant scope. A REAL id belonging to somebody
//     else is the only thing that shows the lookup is scoped.
//
// 08  A ROUND THAT IS A TYPO                -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
//     "reviewRound": 2026. The cap of 20 is a typo guard, not a rule about
//     how many times a school may review somebody. 0 is refused too.
//
// 09  NO ROUND AT ALL                                   -> 201 Created
//     Omit reviewRound entirely and it is round 1, which is what most
//     applications get.
//
// 10  A DUE DATE IN THE PAST                            -> 201 Created
//     "dueAt": "2020-01-01T00:00:00Z". Accepted on purpose: a school
//     catching up on paperwork records a review that was due last week.
//
// 11  A SUSPENDED SCHOOL                   -> 409 SCHOOL_NOT_EDITABLE
//     Refused by the gate BEFORE the form is even looked up.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  POST /schools/current/applications/{id}/assign
//  Run Start an Application first, and Create Staff (or List Staff) for an
//  officer id.
//
//  AN ADMISSION OFFICER OWNS THE FORM; A REVIEWER ASSESSES IT. Different
//  jobs, different endpoints. The officer chases the missing birth
//  certificate, answers the family's calls and makes sure the form does not
//  sit for three weeks.
//
//  IT IS WHAT #24'S OFFICER FILTER READS.
//  ?assignedAdmissionOfficerDocsId=... matched NOTHING for every id until
//  this existed, because nothing could fill the field.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  GIVE IT TO SOMEBODY                                 -> 200 OK
//     THE STATUS DOES NOT MOVE and no date is stamped. That is the
//     difference from Assign a Reviewer, which moves a SUBMITTED form to
//     UNDER_REVIEW because assessment has started. Owning a form is not
//     deciding it.
{
  "assignedAdmissionOfficerDocsId": "{{staffDocsId}}"
}
//
// 02  GIVE IT TO SOMEBODY ELSE                            -> 200 OK
//     Reassigning is the normal case, not an error — people leave, go on
//     holiday and swap workloads. The first officer's worklist loses it.
//
// 03  ASSIGN THE SAME PERSON AGAIN                        -> 200 OK
//     A QUIET 200, unlike Start a Review's second start. The two are
//     different intents: "make sure this is on Anita's list" is worth being
//     idempotent, "pick up work nobody has" is a claim two people cannot
//     both make.
//
// 04  GIVE IT TO NOBODY                     -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
//     THERE IS NO UNASSIGN. The plan has none, and a form belonging to
//     nobody is the state this endpoint exists to get rid of.
// {}
//
// 05  GIVE IT TO A GHOST                       -> 404 STAFF_NOT_FOUND
//     The staff read is SCOPED BY SCHOOL, so another school's staff id
//     answers this too — and that is the one worth sending, because it is a
//     real id somewhere.
// { "assignedAdmissionOfficerDocsId": "6aa39612224c2e933a1cFFFF" }
//
// 06  GIVE AWAY A REJECTED FORM      -> 409 APPLICATION_NOT_ASSIGNABLE
//     Decide it REJECTED first. WITHDRAWN and ENROLLED answer the same: a
//     form is given to somebody so they can move it along, and those have
//     stopped. The message says that rather than just no.
//
// 07  GIVE AWAY A DRAFT                                   -> 200 OK
//     WORTH RUNNING, because Assign a Reviewer refuses one. Nothing to
//     assess yet is not the same as nothing to do — keying a paper form in
//     and chasing the family for what is missing is a real day's work.
//
// 08  GIVE AWAY AN APPROVED FORM                          -> 200 OK
//     The offer is still to come, so it still has an owner. Only the three
//     terminal statuses are refused.
//
// 09  A STALE VERSION                  -> 409 CONCURRENT_MODIFICATION
//     Worth sending on this one: what you would be overwriting is somebody
//     else's decision about who owns this form.
// { "assignedAdmissionOfficerDocsId": "{{staffDocsId}}", "version": 0 }
//
// 10  ANOTHER SCHOOL'S APPLICATION        -> 404 APPLICATION_NOT_FOUND
//     Sign in elsewhere. It still belongs to nobody afterwards.
//
// 11  A SUSPENDED SCHOOL                  -> 409 SCHOOL_NOT_EDITABLE
//     Refused by the gate BEFORE the form is looked up.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  POST /schools/current/applications/{id}/offers
//  Run Start an Application, Submit an Application, then Decide an
//  Application with APPROVED. Set Capacities must list the class.
//
//  THE SCHOOL FORMALLY OFFERS A SEAT, and the family answers with #30.
//  APPROVING IS THE SCHOOL SAYING YES; IT IS NOT THE FAMILY SAYING YES — a
//  family applies to five schools, three approve, and one child arrives.
//  Without a recorded answer a school cannot tell an approved child who is
//  coming from one who went elsewhere, and its seat counts are fiction.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  OFFER A SEAT                                   -> 201 Created
//     ISSUED, with offeredAt stamped and expiresAt defaulted to the ROUND'S
//     enrollment deadline. The application moves to OFFERED as a
//     CONSEQUENCE — nothing asked it to, the same as Assign a Reviewer
//     moving a form to UNDER_REVIEW.
{
  "offeredClassDocsId": "{{schoolClassId}}"
}
//
// 02  OFFER THE SAME FORM AGAIN                          -> 409
//     THE ONE WORTH RUNNING. ONE OFFER LETTER PER ADMISSION: the second is
//     refused and nothing on the form changes.
//
//     WHICH REFUSAL depends on how you got there. Issuing moved the form to
//     OFFERED, and OFFERED is not offerable, so the STATUS answers first
//     with 409 APPLICATION_NOT_ELIGIBLE_FOR_OFFER. 409 OFFER_ALREADY_ISSUED is the
//     guard behind it, for a form that still looks offerable but already
//     has a letter.
//
//     A WITHDRAWN or DECLINED offer does NOT free the slot either — that
//     offer is the application's offer, and its status is the record of
//     what became of it.
//
//     AN EARLIER BUILD SUPERSEDED INSTEAD, which is what the plan asked
//     for. Replaced on 2026-09-23: two documents for one seat is two things
//     to keep in step. SUPERSEDED is now unreachable, like DRAFT.
//
// 03  OFFER A DIFFERENT GRADE                        -> 201 Created
//     The offered class need NOT be the class applied for — a school
//     assesses a child and offers another grade, which is why the offer
//     carries a class of its own.
//
// 04  A CLASS THE ROUND HAS NO SEATS FOR   -> 409 CLASS_NOT_IN_CAPACITY
//     Not in the cycle's seat table. It is the same rule #17 applies to the
//     class applied for. Add it with Set Capacities first.
//
// 05  ANOTHER YEAR'S OR ANOTHER SCHOOL'S CLASS  -> 404 CLASS_NOT_FOUND
//     The class is read in the CYCLE'S academic year and in this school.
//     Another school's class id is a real id somewhere, and this is the
//     refusal worth sending.
//
// 06  OFFER A FORM NOBODY APPROVED    -> 409 APPLICATION_NOT_ELIGIBLE_FOR_OFFER
//     Submit one and offer it without deciding. An offer FOLLOWS a decision
//     rather than making one, and the message sends you to #20.
//
//     APPROVED, WAITLISTED and already-OFFERED all work. WAITLISTED is the
//     "a seat came free" case; OFFERED is what superseding needs.
//     OFFER_ACCEPTED is refused: the family agreed to something specific,
//     and a new revision on top would rewrite that without telling them.
// { "offeredClassDocsId": "{{schoolClassId}}" }
//
// 07  A DEADLINE THAT HAS PASSED    -> 400 OFFER_EXPIRY_IN_THE_PAST
//     An offer nobody could accept is not an offer. THE SAME FIRES WHEN THE
//     CYCLE'S OWN DEADLINE HAS PASSED and the request named no date — the
//     message says which of the two it was.
// { "offeredClassDocsId": "{{schoolClassId}}", "expiresAt": "2020-01-01T00:00:00Z" }
//
// 08  NAME WHO ISSUED IT                             -> 201 Created
//     Optional, because nothing knows who is calling yet. An id that IS
//     sent has to be this school's staff — otherwise 404 STAFF_NOT_FOUND —
//     and the answer names them, from the read that checked them.
// { "offeredClassDocsId": "{{schoolClassId}}", "issuedByDocsId": "{{staffDocsId}}" }
//
// 08b NAME A DEPOSIT INVOICE            -> 404 FEE_INVOICE_NOT_FOUND
//     EVERY ID IS REFUSED TODAY, and that is the point of running it.
//     An id nothing verifies is an id that can be anything — "13212313"
//     was accepted and stored until #29 started looking it up.
//
//     Nothing writes fee_invoices: the finance module has models and no
//     service, so there is no real id to send. Leave the field out.
// { "offeredClassDocsId": "{{schoolClassId}}", "depositInvoiceDocsId": "13212313" }
//
// 09  OVER-OFFER ON PURPOSE                          -> 201 Created
//     Set the seat table to 2 with Set Capacities, then offer to three
//     approved forms. ALL THREE SUCCEED, and that is deliberate: schools
//     offer sixty seats for forty places because a fifth of families go
//     elsewhere, so a refusal at totalSeats would refuse the normal case.
//     Counting offers against places is #7.
//
// 10  NO CLASS AT ALL                     -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
// {}
//
// 11  ANOTHER SCHOOL'S APPLICATION        -> 404 APPLICATION_NOT_FOUND
//     Sign in elsewhere. It gets no offer.
//
// 12  A SUSPENDED SCHOOL                  -> 409 SCHOOL_NOT_EDITABLE
//     Refused by the gate BEFORE the form is looked up.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  PATCH /schools/current/offers/{id}
//  Run Issue an Offer first — it saves admissionOfferDocsId.
//
//  IT EXISTS BECAUSE THE ONE-OFFER RULE OPENED A HOLE. A school issues one
//  letter per admission, so when that letter lapsed nothing could extend it
//  and Issue an Offer would not make another. A FAMILY THAT MISSED THE
//  DEADLINE COULD NOT BE GIVEN A SEAT BY ANY ROUTE.
//
//  EXTENDING A LAPSED OFFER WORKS because nothing writes EXPIRED — a date
//  in the past is what it MEANS — so a lapsed offer is still stored as
//  ISSUED and is still an offer this can reach.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  EXTEND A LAPSED OFFER                               -> 200 OK
//     THE ONE THIS ENDPOINT EXISTS FOR. Let an offer lapse, watch Respond
//     to an Offer answer 409 OFFER_EXPIRED and Issue an Offer refuse a
//     replacement — then send this, and the family can accept again.
{
  "expiresAt": "2099-06-30T00:00:00Z"
}
//
// 02  CORRECT THE GRADE                                   -> 200 OK
//     The same two checks Issue an Offer makes: a class of the CYCLE'S year
//     that the round has seats set up for. A deadline set earlier survives
//     — only what you send moves.
// { "offeredClassDocsId": "{{schoolClassId}}" }
//
// 03  A BODY THAT CHANGES NOTHING           -> 400 NOTHING_TO_UPDATE
//     ASKED FIRST, before the version and before the status — it is the
//     only check about the REQUEST rather than about the world. A version
//     on its own answers this too.
// {}
//
// 04  INTO THE PAST                  -> 400 OFFER_EXPIRY_IN_THE_PAST
//     Extending a lapsed offer is the point; extending it into the past is
//     not an extension. Bringing it FORWARD to a future date is allowed —
//     a school may shorten a window it published.
// { "expiresAt": "2019-01-01T00:00:00Z" }
//
// 05  CORRECT AN ANSWERED OFFER              -> 409 OFFER_NOT_OPEN
//     Respond to an Offer first. Changing the letter under a family would
//     rewrite what they agreed to, and the message says so. A WITHDRAWN one
//     is refused too.
//
// 06  TRY TO ANSWER WITH IT                               -> 200 OK
//     WORTH READING THE ANSWER. status and response are IGNORED — the offer
//     comes back ISSUED with no response. #30 is the only thing that
//     answers for a family, and an edit that could set them would be a
//     second way to say yes on their behalf.
// { "expiresAt": "2099-06-30T00:00:00Z", "status": "ACCEPTED", "response": "ACCEPTED" }
//
// 07  A CLASS THE ROUND HAS NO SEATS FOR -> 409 CLASS_NOT_IN_CAPACITY
//
// 08  A DEPOSIT INVOICE                 -> 404 FEE_INVOICE_NOT_FOUND
//     Every id is refused today — nothing writes fee_invoices.
// { "depositInvoiceDocsId": "13212313" }
//
// 09  A STALE VERSION                  -> 409 CONCURRENT_MODIFICATION
// { "expiresAt": "2099-06-30T00:00:00Z", "version": 0 }
//
// 10  ANOTHER SCHOOL'S OFFER                 -> 404 OFFER_NOT_FOUND
//
// 11  A SUSPENDED SCHOOL                  -> 409 SCHOOL_NOT_EDITABLE
//
//     AND NOTE WHAT DOES NOT MOVE: offeredAt, the offer number and the
//     revision. A correction is not a reissue — this is the same letter.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  POST /schools/current/offers/{id}/respond
//  Run Issue an Offer first — it saves admissionOfferDocsId.
//
//  THIS IS WHY THE OFFER HALF EXISTS. Approving is the SCHOOL saying yes;
//  this is the FAMILY saying yes. Without it a school cannot tell an
//  approved child who is coming from one who went elsewhere.
//
//  IT TAKES THE ANSWER, NOT A STATUS. Two values, which the endpoint maps
//  onto the offer's own seven. Different from Decide an Application, where
//  the school chooses among ITS statuses.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  THE FAMILY ACCEPTS                                   -> 200 OK
//     The offer becomes ACCEPTED, respondedAt is stamped, and THE
//     APPLICATION moves to OFFER_ACCEPTED.
{
  "response": "ACCEPTED"
}
//
// 02  THE FAMILY DECLINES                                  -> 200 OK
//     THE ONE WORTH RUNNING. The offer becomes DECLINED and THE APPLICATION
//     DOES NOT MOVE — read it back with Get an Application and it is still
//     OFFERED. A declined offer is not a rejected applicant: the school
//     decided to admit this child and the family chose otherwise.
// { "response": "DECLINED" }
//
// 03  ANSWER IT TWICE                        -> 409 OFFER_NOT_OPEN
//     An answer is not changed by sending another, and the message says
//     when they answered.
// { "response": "DECLINED" }
//
// 04  WITH A SIGNATURE                                     -> 200 OK
//     NOT VALIDATED, unlike the deposit invoice on Issue an Offer. It
//     points at document_records, which has no service either — but
//     refusing every value on a field the acceptance carries would block
//     the acceptance itself.
// { "response": "ACCEPTED", "acceptanceSignatureDocsId": "67aa15d9dc3f7d0099999992" }
//
// 05  ANSWER A LAPSED OFFER                   -> 409 OFFER_EXPIRED
//     The stored status STILL SAYS ISSUED. Nothing writes EXPIRED — a date
//     in the past is what it means — so only the clock knows, and List
//     Offers with ?expired=true is how a school finds them first.
//
// 06  ANSWER A WITHDRAWN OFFER                -> 409 OFFER_NOT_OPEN
//
// 07  NO ANSWER AT ALL                     -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
// {}
//
// 08  A STALE VERSION                  -> 409 CONCURRENT_MODIFICATION
// { "response": "ACCEPTED", "version": 0 }
//
// 09  ANOTHER SCHOOL'S OFFER                 -> 404 OFFER_NOT_FOUND
//
// 10  A SUSPENDED SCHOOL                  -> 409 SCHOOL_NOT_EDITABLE
//     Refused by the gate BEFORE the offer is looked up.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  POST /schools/current/offers/{id}/withdraw
//  Run Issue an Offer first — it saves admissionOfferDocsId.
//
//  A REASON IS REQUIRED. A seat promised to a family and then taken away is
//  exactly what somebody asks about later, and it is kept on the offer
//  rather than logged and dropped.
//
//  THIS IS WHAT A DELETE WOULD HAVE BEEN. The offer stays and says it was
//  withdrawn and why.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  TAKE IT BACK                                         -> 200 OK
//     NO respondedAt IS STAMPED — the family did not answer, the school
//     changed its mind, and stamping it would make a withdrawal read as a
//     decline in every list that shows that field.
{
  "withdrawalReason": "The class was reorganised and the seat is no longer available."
}
//
// 02  WITHOUT A REASON                     -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
// {}
//
// 03  A BLANK REASON                       -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
// { "withdrawalReason": "   " }
//
// 04  WITHDRAW AN ACCEPTED OFFER            -> 409 OFFER_NOT_OPEN
//     THE ONE WORTH RUNNING. Respond to an Offer with ACCEPTED first. The
//     family holds the seat, and taking it away is a decision about the
//     APPLICATION — #20 — rather than a tidy-up of the letter. The message
//     says so.
// { "withdrawalReason": "Changed our mind." }
//
// 05  WITHDRAW IT TWICE                     -> 409 OFFER_NOT_OPEN
//
// 06  A STALE VERSION                  -> 409 CONCURRENT_MODIFICATION
//     Worth sending here: you may be taking back a seat the family has just
//     accepted.
// { "withdrawalReason": "Reorganised.", "version": 0 }
//
// 07  ANOTHER SCHOOL'S OFFER                 -> 404 OFFER_NOT_FOUND
//
// 08  A SUSPENDED SCHOOL                  -> 409 SCHOOL_NOT_EDITABLE
//
//     AND NOTE WHAT IS NOT CHANGED: the APPLICATION. Withdrawing an offer
//     does not un-approve a child, so the form stays where it is.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  POST /schools/current/applications/{id}/withdraw
//  Run Start an Application first — it saves admissionApplicationDocsId.
//
//  THE FAMILY'S ACT, NOT THE SCHOOL'S. Decide an Application is where a
//  school records what IT decided; this records that the FAMILY stopped. A
//  school that refused a child and a family that went elsewhere are very
//  different numbers at the end of a season.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  THEY WENT ELSEWHERE                                 -> 200 OK
//     withdrawnAt is stamped and decidedAt is NOT — the school decided
//     nothing. The reason lands on withdrawalReason, not decisionNote,
//     which is the school's own word. Two facts, two fields.
{
  "withdrawalReason": "They took a place at another school."
}
//
// 02  AN ABANDONED DRAFT                                  -> 200 OK
//     WORTH RUNNING. A form the family started and never sent can still be
//     withdrawn — it is the one case that needs no other endpoint to have
//     run first. From anywhere before ENROLLED: draft, under review,
//     approved, waitlisted, refused, offered, accepted.
//
// 03  WITHOUT A REASON                     -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
//     A family walking away is what a school learns most from. With nothing
//     said it teaches nobody anything.
// {}
//
// 04  WITHDRAW IT TWICE       -> 409 INVALID_APPLICATION_TRANSITION
//     The message says when they pulled out, and THE FIRST REASON IS NOT
//     OVERWRITTEN.
// { "withdrawalReason": "Again." }
//
// 05  AN ENROLLED FORM        -> 409 INVALID_APPLICATION_TRANSITION
//     The child is a student now. Leaving the school is the student
//     module's business, and writing WITHDRAWN here would leave a register
//     entry pointing at a form that says they never came. #33 is what sets
//     ENROLLED and is not built, so this one needs planting.
//
// 06  WHILE IT HOLDS A LIVE OFFER                         -> 200 OK
//     THE ONE WORTH READING AFTERWARDS. The form withdraws and THE OFFER
//     STAYS ISSUED — so List Offers still shows it, and somebody may ring a
//     family that has gone. This endpoint touches nothing but the
//     application, which is the plan's own collection list.
//
//     Respond to an Offer with DECLINED, or Withdraw an Offer, is what ends
//     the offer. An open review is left alone too: #27d cancels one. Two
//     calls, because each records a different fact.
//
// 07  A STALE VERSION                  -> 409 CONCURRENT_MODIFICATION
// { "withdrawalReason": "They withdrew.", "version": 0 }
//
// 08  ANOTHER SCHOOL'S APPLICATION        -> 404 APPLICATION_NOT_FOUND
//
// 09  A SUSPENDED SCHOOL                  -> 409 SCHOOL_NOT_EDITABLE
//     Refused by the gate BEFORE the form is looked up.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------

{
    "status": "APPROVED",
    "note": "Strong interview, place offered for Grade 7."
}

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  POST /schools/current/applications/{id}/decision
//  Run Session / Sign in, Start an Application, then Submit an Application.
//
//  IT NAMES THE STATUS THE FORM MOVES TO, exactly as #3 does for a cycle.
//  One set of words in and the same set out. The TRANSITION TABLE is what
//  refuses a status this endpoint must not set — not the shape of the body.
//
//  What it can set:  APPROVED   REJECTED   WAITLISTED
//                    ADDITIONAL_INFORMATION_REQUIRED   UNDER_REVIEW
//
//  What it can NEVER set, whatever you send:
//      OFFERED, OFFER_ACCEPTED, ENROLLED   #29, #30 and #33 consequences
//      WITHDRAWN                           #21
//      DRAFT, SUBMITTED                    the family's side
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  APPROVED, WITH NO REVIEW AT ALL                    -> 200 OK
//     The body above, on a freshly submitted form. THE POINT: it never went
//     near #26. Small schools decide in a conversation, and insisting on
//     UNDER_REVIEW would mean assigning a reviewer first — which IS
//     inventing a review row.
//
// 01b APPROVED WHILE SOMEBODY IS STILL LOOKING
//                              -> 409 REVIEWS_STILL_OUTSTANDING
//     THE ONE WORTH RUNNING. Assign a Reviewer first, then send this.
//     THE MESSAGE NAMES THE ROUNDS — "round 1 (PENDING)" — rather than
//     counting them: a count sends somebody hunting, the rounds tell
//     them what to chase.
//
//     Then Complete a Review — or Cancel a Review — and send it again
//     -> 200 OK. A CANCELLED review does not hold an approval up: work
//     the school called off is a settled answer, and waiting for it
//     would mean waiting for something that never happens.
//
//     AND 01 STILL PASSES. Having no reviews and having all of them
//     settled are the same answer to this question — the check reads
//     the OPEN ones, and an empty list is an empty list either way.
// { "status": "APPROVED" }
//
// 01c REJECTED WHILE SOMEBODY IS STILL LOOKING            -> 200 OK
//     The same form, the same open review. ONLY APPROVED IS CHECKED.
//     Refusing, waitlisting and asking for more are all answers a head
//     can give over an incomplete picture — and ADDITIONAL_INFORMATION
//     _REQUIRED is often exactly WHY a review is still open, so
//     blocking it would deadlock the form. Admitting a child is the one
//     decision that claims every assessment was seen.
//
//     AND IT READS THE REVIEWS, NOT THEIR RECOMMENDATIONS. Three
//     reviewers recommending REJECT do not stop an approval, and one
//     recommending APPROVE does not cause one. The rule is that every
//     assessment was SEEN, not that they agreed.
// { "status": "REJECTED", "note": "Not this year." }
//
// 02  REJECTED WITH NO REASON         -> 400 DECISION_NOTE_REQUIRED
//     { "status": "REJECTED" }
//     The form does NOT move. A blank note ("   ") counts as none.
//
// 03  REJECTED, PROPERLY                                 -> 200 OK
//     { "status": "REJECTED",
//       "note": "Interview scores below the cut-off for Grade 7." }
//     The reason is KEPT on decisionNote and reads back on #25 — not logged
//     and thrown away. decidedAt and decisionNote were added to the model
//     with this endpoint, completing the withdrawnAt/withdrawalReason pair.
//
// 04  ASK FOR MORE                                       -> 200 OK
//     { "status": "ADDITIONAL_INFORMATION_REQUIRED",
//       "note": "Last year's report card, please." }
//     The note is required here too — added when this was built, because
//     asking a family for more without saying what tells them nothing.
//
// 05  IT ARRIVED, CARRY ON                               -> 200 OK
//     { "status": "UNDER_REVIEW" }   Run 04 first.
//     The note saying what was asked for SURVIVES.
//
//     THE ONLY STATUS IT WORKS FROM. Try it from SUBMITTED, UNDER_REVIEW or
//     WAITLISTED for the 409. The graph draws this edge and #26 deliberately
//     does not make it: assigning another reviewer is not what decides the
//     information turned up.
//
// 06  A SEAT CAME FREE                                   -> 200 OK
//     WAITLISTED, then APPROVED. Waitlisting twice is 409 — it moves
//     nothing — and the refusal lists APPROVED and REJECTED. Asking a
//     waitlisted family for more is refused too.
//
// 07  A STATUS THIS ENDPOINT MUST NOT SET
//                              -> 409 INVALID_APPLICATION_TRANSITION
//     { "status": "ENROLLED" }
//     THE ONE WORTH RUNNING now that the request names a status. Try
//     OFFERED and OFFER_ACCEPTED too. The transition table is the only
//     thing refusing them, and this is how you see that it does.
//
// 08  DECIDING AN APPROVED FORM AGAIN
//                              -> 409 INVALID_APPLICATION_TRANSITION
//     Approve, then try REJECTED. DELIBERATE: the next thing that happens
//     to an approved applicant is an offer (#29), and changing your mind is
//     withdrawing it (#31). One answer to "what happened to this child".
//     The message sends you to both rather than just saying no.
//
// 09  A FORM NOBODY SENT       -> 409 INVALID_APPLICATION_TRANSITION
//     A DRAFT. The message points at #19.
//
// 10  ANYTHING FINISHED        -> 409 INVALID_APPLICATION_TRANSITION
//     REJECTED, WITHDRAWN, OFFERED, OFFER_ACCEPTED, ENROLLED. Each is told
//     WHY it can be moved nowhere rather than shown an empty list.
//
// 11  A STALE VERSION                -> 409 CONCURRENT_MODIFICATION
//     { "status": "APPROVED", "version": 0 }
//     Read the form on #25 first and note its version. #17, #19, #20 and
//     #25 all RETURN version as of 2026-09-22 — before that the field was
//     accepted and there was no way to learn its value.
//
// 12  A SUSPENDED SCHOOL             -> 409 SCHOOL_NOT_EDITABLE
//     Refused by the gate BEFORE the form is looked up.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  GET /schools/current/reviews
//  A GET has no body; the cases are the query parameters below.
//
//  A REVIEWER'S OWN QUEUE. The first two filters ARE the index:
//  school_reviewer_status_due_idx is
//  {schoolId, reviewerDocsId, status, dueAt} — one person, one state,
//  soonest first. That is what this endpoint is named for.
//
//  THERE IS NO "ME". Nothing in this project knows who is calling yet, so
//  whose queue it is has to be said out loud.
//
//  NO GATES. A suspended school still sees what it owes.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  EVERYTHING                                           -> 200 OK
//     All filters disabled. Soonest due first — and note that reviews with
//     NO due date come FIRST, because Mongo puts a missing field before
//     every value in an ascending sort. That is the wrong end of a queue,
//     and case 03 is the answer to it rather than the order.
//
// 02  ONE PERSON'S QUEUE                                   -> 200 OK
//     ?reviewerDocsId=...&status=PENDING   The index, in its order.
//
// 03  WHAT IS LATE                    ?overdue=true        -> 200 OK
//     TWO CONDITIONS, NOT ONE: past its due date AND still PENDING or
//     IN_PROGRESS.
//
//     THE ONE WORTH RUNNING: take a review whose due date has passed, look
//     at it here, then COMPLETE it with #27 and look again. It LEAVES this
//     list. A one-condition filter would still be showing it, and the
//     difference is invisible until you try exactly that.
//
// 04  A REVIEW WITH NO DUE DATE       ?overdue=true        -> 200 OK
//     Assign one without dueAt. It is NEVER overdue — $lt does not match a
//     missing field, so it falls out of the query rather than needing a
//     rule. ?overdue=false returns it.
//
// 05  ONE FORM'S REVIEWS                                   -> 200 OK
//     ?admissionApplicationDocsId=...  For walking down from an application
//     rather than across from a person.
//
// 06  PAGE ONE AT A TIME                                   -> 200 OK
//     Assign six reviews to one form with NO due date — three reviewers
//     across rounds 1 and 2 — then ?size=1 and walk. No row appears twice.
//
//     THAT FIXTURE IS THE POINT. A review has no unique business key (its
//     uniqueness is the triple of application, round and reviewer), so the
//     document id is the tiebreaker. Rows with DIFFERENT due dates are
//     already ordered and prove nothing.
//
// 07  SORT BY WHAT A REVIEWER WROTE  -> 400 INVALID_SORT_FIELD
//     ?sort=notes and ?sort=criterionScores. Ordering is a read: sort by a
//     field and walk the pages and you learn its values even where nothing
//     displays them. Allowed: dueAt, completedAt, reviewRound, status,
//     score, createdAt, updatedAt.
//
// 08  A DIRECTION THAT IS NOT ONE
//       ?sort=dueAt,sideways         -> 400 INVALID_SORT_DIRECTION
//
// 09  SIZE OVER THE CAP    ?size=101           -> 400 INVALID_PAGE_SIZE
// 10  A NEGATIVE PAGE      ?page=-1                 -> 400 INVALID_PAGE
//
// 11  A SUSPENDED SCHOOL STILL READS                       -> 200 OK
//     Record a Review answers 409 for the same school.
//
// 12  ANOTHER SCHOOL'S QUEUE                               -> 200 OK
//     Sign in elsewhere. None of this school's reviews appear.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  POST /schools/current/reviews/{id}/start
//  Run Assign a Reviewer first — it saves admissionReviewDocsId.
//  NO BODY. The id in the path is the whole request.
//
//  THE REVIEWER HAS PICKED IT UP. #27 can make the same move inside a
//  general edit; this exists because STARTING is an event rather than a
//  field being set, and this module gives events a verb — the same call
//  #19 and #3 make. In the API tester, opening a review fires it on its own.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  PICK UP A PENDING REVIEW                            -> 200 OK
//     -> IN_PROGRESS. NOTHING ELSE MOVES: no score, no recommendation, and
//     no completedAt — starting is not finishing.
//
// 02  START IT AGAIN          -> 409 INVALID_REVIEW_TRANSITION
//     THE ONE WORTH RUNNING. Not idempotent on purpose: the caller believed
//     they were picking up work nobody had, and a silent 200 would hide
//     that two people are on the same review.
//
// 03  START A COMPLETED ONE    -> 409 REVIEW_ALREADY_COMPLETED
//     Complete it with Record a Review first. The message sends you to #26
//     to assign another rather than just refusing.
//
// 04  START A CANCELLED ONE            -> 409 REVIEW_CANCELLED
//
//     THOSE ARE #27'S OWN CODES, not new ones. A caller should not have to
//     learn two vocabularies for "this review is finished".
//
//     AND NOTE WHAT IS NOT HERE: a review is never APPROVED or REJECTED.
//     Those are the APPLICATION's status (#20) and the reviewer's
//     RECOMMENDATION, which is a different field on the same document.
//     AdmissionReviewStatus has four values and this guards all four.
//
// 05  ANOTHER SCHOOL'S REVIEW           -> 404 REVIEW_NOT_FOUND
//     Sign in elsewhere. It stays PENDING.
//
// 06  A SUSPENDED SCHOOL              -> 409 SCHOOL_NOT_EDITABLE
//     Refused by the gate BEFORE the review is looked up. List Reviews on
//     the same school still answers 200.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  POST /schools/current/reviews/{id}/complete
//  Run Assign a Reviewer first — it saves admissionReviewDocsId.
//
//  THE REVIEWER IS FINISHED, AND THIS IS WHAT THEY CONCLUDED. #27 can make
//  the same move inside a general edit; this exists because FINISHING is an
//  event rather than a field being set, and this module gives events a verb
//  — the same call #27b, #19 and #3 make.
//
//  THERE IS NO STATUS FIELD. The status is the endpoint. A body naming one
//  would be a second way to say the same thing, and a way to disagree with
//  the path.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  FINISH IT                                           -> 200 OK
//     The whole result in one call. completedAt is stamped HERE and nowhere
//     else in this module — not by #27b, and not by a cancellation.
{
  "recommendation": "APPROVE",
  "score": 86.50,
  "criterionScores": { "INTERVIEW": 42.50, "ENTRANCE_TEST": 44.00 },
  "notes": "Strong in the interaction, comfortably above the mark."
}
//
// 02  JUST THE RECOMMENDATION                             -> 200 OK
//     Everything else is optional, and a score saved earlier with Record a
//     Review survives. Only what you send moves.
// { "recommendation": "WAITLIST" }
//
// 03  NO RECOMMENDATION AT ALL       -> 400 RECOMMENDATION_REQUIRED
//     THE ONE WORTH RUNNING, on a review that has never had one. It is the
//     one thing a review exists to produce.
// {}
//
// 04  EMPTY BODY, RECOMMENDATION ALREADY SAVED            -> 200 OK
//     Save one with Record a Review first, then send {} here. The rule is
//     that the REVIEW says what it recommends by the time it is done — not
//     that THIS request carries it. Nobody sends it twice.
// {}
//
//     AND NOTE WHAT IS NOT REFUSED: there is no NOTHING_TO_UPDATE on this
//     endpoint. That is the difference between a verb and a PATCH — an empty
//     body here still asks for the move the path names.
//
// 05  COMPLETE IT TWICE             -> 409 REVIEW_ALREADY_COMPLETED
//     COMPLETED is terminal. A result recorded wrongly is corrected by
//     Cancel a Review and assigning another with #26, which leaves BOTH in
//     the history rather than quietly overwriting one.
// { "recommendation": "REJECT" }
//
// 06  COMPLETE A CANCELLED ONE               -> 409 REVIEW_CANCELLED
// { "recommendation": "APPROVE" }
//
// 07  CLEAR THE CRITERIA WHILE FINISHING                  -> 200 OK
//     {} REPLACES the map with nothing. Leaving the field out is the other
//     thing entirely — it keeps what is there. Merging would leave no way to
//     remove a criterion recorded by mistake.
// { "recommendation": "APPROVE", "criterionScores": {} }
//
// 08  A STALE VERSION                  -> 409 CONCURRENT_MODIFICATION
//     Read the review with Get an Application first, then send a version one
//     behind. Leave version out and last write wins.
// { "recommendation": "APPROVE", "version": 0 }
//
// 09  A NEGATIVE SCORE                       -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
//     A typo rather than a scale. There is NO upper bound — out of 100, out
//     of 50 or out of 5 is the school's business, not the API's.
// { "recommendation": "APPROVE", "score": -1 }
//
// 10  APPROVED INSTEAD OF APPROVE            -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
//     APPROVED is the APPLICATION's word (#20). A reviewer RECOMMENDS, and
//     the four values are APPROVE, REJECT, WAITLIST, REQUEST_MORE_INFORMATION.
// { "recommendation": "APPROVED" }
//
// 11  A SCORE THAT IS NOT A NUMBER          -> 400 MALFORMED_REQUEST
//     The JSON reader refuses it before the endpoint runs, so it beats even
//     REVIEW_ALREADY_COMPLETED. Not reachable from the tester, whose boxes
//     are type="number" — this is where it is sent from.
// { "recommendation": "APPROVE", "score": "eighty six" }
//
// 12  ANOTHER SCHOOL'S REVIEW               -> 404 REVIEW_NOT_FOUND
//     Sign in elsewhere. It stays where it was.
// { "recommendation": "APPROVE" }
//
// 13  A SUSPENDED SCHOOL                  -> 409 SCHOOL_NOT_EDITABLE
//     Refused by the gate BEFORE the review is looked up.
// { "recommendation": "APPROVE" }
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  POST /schools/current/reviews/{id}/cancel
//  Run Assign a Reviewer first — it saves admissionReviewDocsId.
//
//  THIS IS WHAT A DELETE WOULD HAVE BEEN, AND IT IS NOT ONE. There is no
//  DELETE on this collection. Admissions keeps what it decided, including
//  who it asked and that it changed its mind — so the review stays, and says
//  it was called off and why.
//
//  AND A PENDING ROW NOBODY WILL EVER WORK IS WORSE THAN A CANCELLED ONE:
//  it sits in List Reviews for ever and makes the backlog a lie.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  CALL OFF A PENDING ROW                              -> 200 OK
//     The commonest case. completedAt is NOT stamped — a cancelled review
//     was not completed, however much of it was filled in.
{
  "notes": "The reviewer has left the school, so this round is being reassigned."
}
//
// 02  CANCEL ONE SOMEBODY HAD STARTED                     -> 200 OK
//     Start a Review first, then record a score. WHATEVER WAS RECORDED SO
//     FAR STAYS — that is the history the cancellation is written into.
// { "notes": "Round withdrawn after the family moved city." }
//
// 03  NO REASON AT ALL            -> 400 CANCELLATION_NOTE_REQUIRED
//     THE ONE WORTH RUNNING, on a review with no notes. Work called off with
//     nothing said is a gap in the record — the same reading that makes
//     lostReason required on a lost inquiry.
// {}
//
// 04  A BLANK REASON              -> 400 CANCELLATION_NOTE_REQUIRED
//     Spaces are not a reason. blankToNull turns it into nothing before the
//     check, as everywhere in this project.
// { "notes": "   " }
//
// 05  EMPTY BODY, NOTES ALREADY ON THE REVIEW             -> 200 OK
//     Record a note with Record a Review first. The REVIEW's notes count, as
//     the recommendation does on Complete a Review — and sending nothing
//     KEEPS them rather than blanking them.
// {}
//
// 06  CANCEL A COMPLETED ONE       -> 409 REVIEW_ALREADY_COMPLETED
//     What somebody found is a record. The school undoes it by DECIDING
//     differently in #20, not by erasing the review.
// { "notes": "Wrong reviewer." }
//
// 07  CANCEL IT TWICE                        -> 409 REVIEW_CANCELLED
// { "notes": "Again." }
//
// 08  A STALE VERSION                  -> 409 CONCURRENT_MODIFICATION
//     WORTH SENDING ON THIS ONE: somebody may have just FINISHED the work
//     you are calling off, and the version is what stops the cancellation
//     landing on top of it.
// { "notes": "Reassigning.", "version": 0 }
//
// 09  A REASON OVER 2000 CHARACTERS          -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
//
// 10  ANOTHER SCHOOL'S REVIEW               -> 404 REVIEW_NOT_FOUND
//     Sign in elsewhere. It stays where it was.
// { "notes": "Reassigning." }
//
// 11  A SUSPENDED SCHOOL                  -> 409 SCHOOL_NOT_EDITABLE
//     Refused by the gate BEFORE the review is looked up.
// { "notes": "Reassigning." }
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------

{
    "status": "COMPLETED",
    "score": 86.50,
    "recommendation": "APPROVE",
    "criterionScores": { "INTERVIEW": 42.50, "ENTRANCE_TEST": 44.00 },
    "notes": "The applicant performed well in the interaction."
}

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  PATCH /schools/current/reviews/{id}
//  Run Assign a Reviewer first — it saves admissionReviewDocsId.
//
//  ONLY WHAT YOU SEND MOVES. Every field is optional, so a reviewer can save
//  a score today and add the recommendation tomorrow. A body carrying
//  nothing is 400 NOTHING_TO_UPDATE.
//
//  ADDRESSED BY ITS OWN ID, not under the application — a reviewer opens
//  their own queue far more often than they walk down from a form.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  A SCORE, AND NOTHING ELSE                          -> 200 OK
//     { "score": 86.50 }
//     Still PENDING afterwards. A score is not a completion, which is what
//     lets a reviewer save as they go.
//
// 02  COMPLETE IT WITH NO RECOMMENDATION
//                                -> 400 RECOMMENDATION_REQUIRED
//     { "status": "COMPLETED" }   The review does NOT move.
//     A finished review that does not say what it recommends is the one
//     thing a review exists to produce.
//
// 03  COMPLETE IT PROPERLY                               -> 200 OK
//     The body above. completedAt is stamped, and from here the review can
//     never change again.
//
// 04  EDIT IT AFTERWARDS          -> 409 REVIEW_ALREADY_COMPLETED
//     { "score": 99 }   THE ONE WORTH RUNNING. The message tells you to
//     cancel this review and assign another, which leaves BOTH in the
//     history rather than quietly overwriting one.
//
// 04b A SCORE THAT IS NOT A NUMBER      -> 400 MALFORMED_REQUEST
//     { "criterionScores": { "INTERVIEW": "abc" } }
//     Refused by the JSON reader BEFORE the endpoint runs, so it beats
//     even REVIEW_ALREADY_COMPLETED on a finished review. Send it here:
//     the API tester's score box is a number field and cannot type it.
//
// 05  CRITERIA REPLACE, THEY DO NOT MERGE                -> 200 OK
//     Send { "criterionScores": { "INTERVIEW": 42.5, "ENTRANCE_TEST": 44 } }
//     then  { "criterionScores": { "INTERVIEW": 40 } }
//     ONE key is left, not two. A map is one value, and merging would leave
//     no way to remove a criterion recorded by mistake. {} clears it and it
//     is then left OFF the response entirely.
//
// 06  CANCEL WITH NO REASON    -> 400 CANCELLATION_NOTE_REQUIRED
//     { "status": "CANCELLED" }   Work called off with no reason is a gap
//     in the record — the same reading that makes lostReason required.
//
//     A cancelled review gets NO completedAt. It was not completed, however
//     much of it was filled in.
//
// 07  AN EMPTY BODY                    -> 400 NOTHING_TO_UPDATE
//     {}  — and { "version": 5 } alone is the SAME answer. The request's
//     own shape is checked before the state of the world.
//
// 08  GOING BACKWARDS           -> 409 INVALID_REVIEW_TRANSITION
//     { "status": "PENDING" } on an IN_PROGRESS review. It only runs
//     forwards, and the refusal lists what IS reachable.
//
//     PENDING -> COMPLETED skips IN_PROGRESS on purpose: most reviews are
//     done in one sitting, and an "I have started" call nobody would keep
//     up with is ceremony rather than a record.
//
// 09  A STALE VERSION                -> 409 CONCURRENT_MODIFICATION
//     { "score": 10, "version": 0 }  Read it on List Reviews first.
//
// 10  ANOTHER SCHOOL'S REVIEW          -> 404 REVIEW_NOT_FOUND
//     Sign in elsewhere. Never a 200 — a score written against it would be
//     this school's mark on another school's child.
//
// 11  A SUSPENDED SCHOOL             -> 409 SCHOOL_NOT_EDITABLE
//     Refused by the gate BEFORE the review is looked up. List Reviews on
//     the same school still answers 200.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  POST /schools/current/inquiries
//  Run Session / Sign in first. The academic year must exist.
//
//  ALMOST EVERYTHING IS OPTIONAL, and that is the endpoint's whole
//  character. A phone call is "a mother rang about her son for next year" —
//  a name, a year, and nothing else. An endpoint that demanded a date of
//  birth and a guardian's email would be REFUSING THE COMMONEST LEAD THERE
//  IS, and the front desk would stop using it.
//
//  WHAT IT UNBLOCKED: until #8 existed, inquiries had no controller at all.
//  Yet Start an Application moves a named lead to APPLICATION_STARTED and
//  Submit moves it to APPLICATION_SUBMITTED — two write paths in built
//  endpoints that no API call could reach.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  A NAME AND A YEAR                              -> 201 Created
//     THE COMMONEST LEAD THERE IS. No date of birth, no guardian, no class.
//     It comes back NEW with a generated INQ/ number.
{
  "prospectiveStudentName": "Aarav Sharma",
  "academicYear": "{{academicYear}}"
}
//
// 02  THE WHOLE FORM                                 -> 201 Created
//     When the desk has it all. The class and the counsellor come back
//     NAMED, not just as ids.
// {
//   "prospectiveStudentName": "Aarav Sharma",
//   "academicYear": "{{academicYear}}",
//   "dateOfBirth": "2020-04-11",
//   "gender": "MALE",
//   "interestedClassDocsId": "{{schoolClassId}}",
//   "assignedCounselorDocsId": "{{staffDocsId}}",
//   "source": "WALK_IN",
//   "sourceDetails": "Saw the hoarding on the main road",
//   "notes": "Wants a school bus on the east route.",
//   "guardians": [{ "fullName": "Priya Sharma", "relation": "MOTHER",
//                   "phoneNumber": "9000000001", "primaryContact": true }]
// }
//
// 03  A GUARDIAN WITH ONLY A PHONE NUMBER            -> 201 Created
//     WORTH RUNNING. No name and no relation — an APPLICATION would refuse
//     that, because the family filled a form in. A LEAD must not: the desk
//     writes down a number and a first name.
//
//     That number is what #15 searches on to answer "is this family already
//     known", and it can only find the ones who left one.
// { "prospectiveStudentName": "Unknown child", "academicYear": "{{academicYear}}", "guardians": [{ "phoneNumber": "9000000002" }] }
//
// 04  TWO CHILDREN, ONE PHONE NUMBER                 -> 201 Created
//     IT DOES NOT REFUSE DUPLICATES, and it should not. #15 asks "do we
//     know them" BEFORE this, and the person at the desk decides. Refusing
//     here would mean guessing that two children sharing a number are one
//     enquiry — which a family with two children is not.
//
// 05  NO NAME                             -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
// { "academicYear": "{{academicYear}}" }
//
// 06  NO YEAR                             -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
//     Those two are all it requires: a lead about nobody is not a lead, and
//     a lead is always FOR an intake.
// { "prospectiveStudentName": "Aarav Sharma" }
//
// 07  A YEAR THE SCHOOL DOES NOT HAVE  -> 404 ACADEMIC_YEAR_NOT_FOUND
//     It must exist, but it NEED NOT be the running one — a lead is about
//     the future, which is the normal case rather than the edge.
// { "prospectiveStudentName": "Aarav Sharma", "academicYear": "1999-2000" }
//
// 08  A CLASS OF ANOTHER YEAR         -> 409 CLASS_NOT_IN_CYCLE_YEAR
//     Another school's class id answers this too, and THAT is the one worth
//     sending — it is a real id somewhere, so it is the version that proves
//     the lookup is scoped.
// { "prospectiveStudentName": "Aarav Sharma", "academicYear": "{{academicYear}}", "interestedClassDocsId": "6aa39612224c2e933a1cFFFF" }
//
// 09  A COUNSELLOR WHO IS NOT STAFF        -> 404 STAFF_NOT_FOUND
// { "prospectiveStudentName": "Aarav Sharma", "academicYear": "{{academicYear}}", "assignedCounselorDocsId": "6aa39612224c2e933a1cFFFF" }
//
// 10  A BIRTHDAY IN THE FUTURE          -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
// { "prospectiveStudentName": "Aarav Sharma", "academicYear": "{{academicYear}}", "dateOfBirth": "2099-01-01" }
//
// 11  A SUSPENDED SCHOOL                -> 409 SCHOOL_NOT_EDITABLE
//     Refused by the gate BEFORE the year is looked up.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  PATCH /schools/current/inquiries/{inquiryId}
//  Correct what the front desk misheard.
//
//  A LEAD IS THE SCHOOL'S OWN NOTES, NOT A DECLARATION THE FAMILY SIGNED.
//  That one sentence is what the whole endpoint follows from — and it is
//  the difference between this and Correct an Application.
//
//  THERE IS NO STATUS GATE. #18 refuses anything but a DRAFT application,
//  because Submit freezes a snapshot of what the family declared. Nobody
//  declares a lead: somebody took a phone call and wrote down what they
//  heard, and the commonest thing that happens to a phone call is
//  mishearing it. A LOST lead can still have a misspelt name put right.
//
//  A BLANK CLEARS AN OPTIONAL FIELD; an absent one leaves it alone. A
//  REQUIRED field refuses a blank instead. dateOfBirth and gender cannot
//  be cleared at all — neither is a string, so neither has a blank to
//  send. That is a gap, said out loud rather than papered over.
//
//  MOVING THE YEAR RE-CHECKS THE CLASS, INCLUDING ONE NOBODY MENTIONED.
//  A lead's interested class must be a class of the year it is about, and
//  a year that moved and left an unrelated class behind would break that
//  silently. Case 08 is the one worth running.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  THE MISHEARD NAME                               -> 200 OK
//     WHAT THE ENDPOINT EXISTS FOR. Nothing else moves — the notes, the
//     class and the guardians are all still there afterwards.
{
  "prospectiveStudentName": "Aarav Sharma"
}
//
// 02  CLEAR THE NOTES                                 -> 200 OK
//     "" CLEARS AN OPTIONAL FIELD. It comes back ABSENT, not as an empty
//     string. Without this a note typed by mistake would be permanent.
// { "notes": "" }
//
// 03  THEY NO LONGER HAVE A CLASS IN MIND             -> 200 OK
// { "interestedClassDocsId": "" }
//
// 04  A BLANK NAME                        -> 400 BLANK_STUDENT_NAME
//     REQUIRED FIELDS REFUSE A BLANK. "" here is somebody trying to remove
//     a name the document must carry.
// { "prospectiveStudentName": "" }
//
// 05  A BODY THAT ASKS FOR NOTHING        -> 400 NOTHING_TO_UPDATE
//     A version ALONE counts as nothing — it is not a change. And the
//     check runs BEFORE the version, so a stale one cannot mask it.
// { }
//
// 06  REPLACE THE GUARDIANS                           -> 200 OK
//     REPLACED WHOLE, never merged. There is no id on a guardian to merge
//     by — they are embedded, not documents.
// { "guardians": [{ "fullName": "Priya Sharma", "relation": "MOTHER",
//                   "phoneNumber": "9000000001", "primaryContact": true }] }
//
// 07  CLEAR THE GUARDIANS                             -> 200 OK
//     ALLOWED HERE, REFUSED BY #18. An application with no guardian is not
//     one a school can act on; a LEAD with none is the walk-in who gave a
//     child's name and left, which Capture a Lead is built to accept.
// { "guardians": [] }
//
// 08  MOVE THE YEAR ON A LEAD THAT HAS A CLASS
//                                     -> 409 CLASS_NOT_IN_CYCLE_YEAR
//     THE ONE WORTH RUNNING. The class is never mentioned in this body and
//     is re-checked anyway. The refusal names the two ways out.
// { "academicYear": "2027-2028" }
//
// 09  MOVE THE YEAR AND CLEAR THE CLASS               -> 200 OK
//     One of the two ways out.
// { "academicYear": "2027-2028", "interestedClassDocsId": "" }
//
// 10  A YEAR THE SCHOOL DOES NOT HAVE  -> 404 ACADEMIC_YEAR_NOT_FOUND
// { "academicYear": "1999-2000" }
//
// 11  ANOTHER SCHOOL'S CLASS           -> 409 CLASS_NOT_IN_CYCLE_YEAR
//     A REAL ID, AND STILL REFUSED. The lookup is scoped by school AND by
//     year, and a nonexistent id would prove neither.
// { "interestedClassDocsId": "6aa39612224c2e933a1cFFFF" }
//
// 12  FIELDS ANOTHER ENDPOINT OWNS      -> 200 OK, and none of them move
//     WORTH RUNNING. status is #12's, the counsellor is #11's, the chase
//     date is #10's. All three are IGNORED, not refused — Jackson drops
//     unknown fields. Read the response and see the lead unmoved.
// { "notes": "still here", "status": "LOST",
//   "assignedCounselorDocsId": "{{staffDocsId}}",
//   "nextFollowUpAt": "2030-01-01T00:00:00Z" }
//
// 13  A LOST LEAD                                     -> 200 OK
//     NO STATUS GATE. Move one to LOST directly in the database, then
//     correct it. Correct an Application would refuse the equivalent.
// { "prospectiveStudentName": "Aarav Sharma" }
//
// 14  A STALE VERSION                -> 409 CONCURRENT_MODIFICATION
// { "notes": "Wants the east bus route.", "version": 1 }
//
// 15  A BIRTHDAY IN THE FUTURE          -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
// { "dateOfBirth": "2099-01-01" }
//
// 16  ANOTHER SCHOOL'S LEAD               -> 404 INQUIRY_NOT_FOUND
//     A 403 would confirm it exists.
// { "prospectiveStudentName": "Hijacked" }
//
// 17  A SUSPENDED SCHOOL                -> 409 SCHOOL_NOT_EDITABLE
//     Refused by the gate BEFORE the lead is even looked up.
// { "notes": "x" }

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  GET /schools/current/inquiries
//  The counsellor's worklist. Soonest to chase first.
//
//  OVERDUE IS TWO CONDITIONS, NOT ONE: past its follow-up date AND not
//  LOST or CLOSED. A lead somebody gave up on last month has a past date
//  too, and nobody owes it a phone call.
//
//  A LEAD WITH NO nextFollowUpAt IS NEVER OVERDUE. $lt does not match a
//  missing field — so it falls out of the query rather than needing a rule,
//  and it sorts to the FRONT by default, because Mongo puts a missing field
//  before every value.
//
//  THERE IS NO "MINE". Nothing knows who is asking yet, so whose worklist
//  it is has to be named in the query.
//
//  A row is thinner than the lead: no notes, no source details, no
//  timeline. But the PHONE NUMBER is on it — the point of a worklist is to
//  pick the phone up. Get One Lead is where the rest is.
//
//  Every parameter is a QUERY parameter. Enable them one at a time.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  THE WHOLE WORKLIST                              -> 200 OK
//     No filter. Soonest to chase first.
//
// 02  WHAT IS LATE                     ?overdue=true  -> 200 OK
//     PAST ITS DATE AND STILL OPEN.
//
// 03  THE MIRROR                      ?overdue=false  -> 200 OK
//     And it INCLUDES the lost ones and the ones with no date at all.
//     "Not late" is not the same as "still open".
//
// 04  ONE COUNSELLOR'S OPEN LEADS                     -> 200 OK
//     ?status=CONTACTED&assignedCounselorDocsId=...
//     The two keys school_inquiry_pipeline_idx leads with, in its order.
//
// 05  BY THE INQUIRY NUMBER      ?search=INQ/2026/...  -> 200 OK
//     The note on the pad carries a number, the parent on the phone gives
//     a name. Both work, anywhere in the field, ignoring case.
//
// 06  A REGULAR EXPRESSION               ?search=.*   -> 200 OK, none found
//     THE NEEDLE IS QUOTED. It matches the literal two characters, not
//     every lead in the school.
//
// 07  SORT BY THE NOTES              ?sort=notes      -> 400 INVALID_SORT_FIELD
//     AN ALLOWLIST IS A SECURITY CONTROL: ordering is a read, and paging a
//     sorted field walks its values out — here, everything a counsellor
//     ever wrote about a family. notes, lostReason, sourceDetails,
//     guardians and schoolId are all refused.
//
// 08  A SIZE OVER 100                    ?size=101    -> 400 INVALID_PAGE_SIZE
//
// 09  A SUSPENDED SCHOOL                              -> 200 OK
//     A READ RUNS NO GATES. A school that cannot be edited still owes
//     these families a call back.

// =========================================================================
//  TEST CASES  —  GET /schools/current/inquiries/{inquiryId}
//  One lead with its whole timeline.
//
//  EVERYTHING A WORKLIST ROW LEAVES OFF: the notes, where the lead came
//  from, why it was lost — and every follow-up in the order it happened,
//  with whoever logged it NAMED.
//
//  OLDEST FIRST, because a conversation reads forwards. Sorted by the
//  server rather than trusted: a $push is not a promise about order once
//  anything else touches the array.
//
//  ONE STAFF QUERY FOR THE WHOLE LEAD. The counsellor it is assigned to and
//  everybody who logged a follow-up are asked about together — a timeline
//  of ten calls by three people is one read, not ten. And it is
//  SCHOOL-SCOPED, so another school's real staff id is not named either.
//
//  NAMES ARE RESOLVED TOLERANTLY. A class that was removed, or a counsellor
//  who has left, leaves the name off and the lead readable. The call they
//  made still happened.
//
//  The id goes in the PATH. Swap {{inquiryDocsId}} for the cases below.
// =========================================================================
//
// 01  A LEAD JUST CAPTURED                            -> 200 OK
//     followUps is an EMPTY LIST, not absent — #10 logs the first entry
//     and is not built, so this is true of every lead in the system.
//
// 02  ONE WITH A TIMELINE                             -> 200 OK
//     OLDEST FIRST, each entry naming who logged it. Worth reading against
//     List Inquiries' row, which carries none of it.
//
// 03  AN ID THAT DOES NOT EXIST                       -> 404 INQUIRY_NOT_FOUND
//
// 04  ANOTHER SCHOOL'S LEAD                           -> 404 INQUIRY_NOT_FOUND
//     A REAL ID, AND STILL A 404. A 403 would confirm it exists. The read
//     is scoped by school IN THE QUERY, never checked after.
//
// 05  A SUSPENDED SCHOOL                              -> 200 OK
//     A READ RUNS NO GATES.
